      "narrative": "Alsym Energy is a Series C climate and energy technology company that has raised approximately $110\u2013111M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private companies and one public company (Lnza) operating in the same sector, with primary peer references including KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses total capital raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C-to-next-stage step-ups, yielding $187M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage companies: KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M. The median valuation across this set is $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These disparate approaches reflect the wide dispersion in public market comparables and early-stage private valuations within frontier energy.\n\nThe two methods imply a triangulated valuation range of $159M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $594M. The median provides a reasonable midpoint estimate but should be treated with caution given the substantial spread between stage-progression and peer-median results. Key uncertainties include the maturity and commercialization timeline of Alsym's technology relative to its peer set, the degree to which peer valuations reflect speculative capital allocation in the climate tech sector, and the absence of near-term profitability milestones in the data. The wide range underscores the sensitivity of frontier-tech valuations to technology risk and market-adoption assumptions.",
