      "narrative": "Ursa Space Systems is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised approximately $67M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 6 private companies at Series B through Series D stages, alongside 5 public comparables in the Space & Aerospace sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate the company's fair value. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $114M based on total capital raised as proxy. Peer-median methodology across 6 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies yields $1.8B, with the peer set ranging from $1.15B (floor) to $8.0B (Sierra Space at Series C). The peer cohort includes Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B, Series D), and Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to unavailable revenue data for the target.\n\nThe triangulated range supports a valuation of $97M to $2.1B, with a median of $952M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression yields a significantly lower result than peer medians, suggesting either that Ursa occupies a distinct risk profile within the space sector or that private comps at this stage command significant premiums over capital deployed. Key sensitivities include revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and technical differentiation relative to the peer set. Further diligence on near-term revenue visibility and capital efficiency would narrow this range substantially.",
