      "narrative": "AheadComputing is a Seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Debbie Marr, Mark Dechene, Jonathan Pearce, and Srikanth Srinivasan that has raised $51.5M to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector includes 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers, though a sufficiently narrow same-stage peer set does not exist for reliable median benchmarking.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($51.5M) as a proxy for entry valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the next financing stage yields $129M. The Peer-Median approach was not viable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables in the Chips & Semiconductors universe. Public-Comp Anchoring could not be executed because AheadComputing's revenue is not on file, preventing application of the 21.0x P/S median observed across the three public semiconductor comps.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $109M to $148M, centered at $129M. This range reflects high uncertainty inherent in single-method triangulation. Key risks include the absence of direct peer benchmarks at seed maturity, unknown revenue run rate, and the known volatility of semiconductor valuations tied to capital intensity and technology inflection cycles. Additional disclosure of commercial metrics would narrow this range materially.",
