      "narrative": "1872 is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of nine private robotics firms and one public comparable (277810.KQ), though the narrow peer set limits methodological breadth.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the primary applicable method, applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement. This yields an implied valuation of $38M. A peer-median approach could not be applied: while ten same-sector peers exist, fewer than three occupy the same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier, making median benchmarking statistically unreliable without risking misleading anchoring to a broader, less comparable cohort.\n\nThe triangulated range is $32M (low), $38M (median), to $43M (high), derived from the single applicable method. This narrow methodological foundation reflects genuine data constraints rather than convergence across methods. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of a 2.5x stage multiplier to 1872's specific subsector dynamics, the relevance of the ten identified robotics comps given heterogeneity in application domain and technology maturity, and whether total capital raised is a reliable proxy for intrinsic value at seed stage. Additional comparable transactions or margin-of-safety adjustments for execution risk would strengthen conviction in this range.",
