      "narrative": "Electric Era, a Series A climate and energy company founded by Quincy Lee, has raised $11.5M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of nine same-sector peers (one public, eight private), though narrow-band peer matching\u2014filtering for identical stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier\u2014yielded insufficient datapoints to support a median-based multiple.\n\nThe stage-progression method was therefore applied as the primary valuation anchor. Using total capital raised ($11.5M, rounded to $12M) as a proxy for post-money Series A valuation, a 2.0x step-up multiplier to notional Series B entry yields $23M. This multiplier reflects typical venture capital progression dynamics between institutional early rounds.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $20M to $26M, with a median of $23M. This assessment carries material uncertainty: the lack of three or more same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables in the Climate & Energy sector limits validation through peer median methods. Key sensitivities include actual post-money Series A terms (which could shift the base), stage-up timing and market conditions, and company-specific unit economics relative to the Helion, Redwood Materials, and Electric Hydrogen cohort. Additional disclosure of revenue, burn rate, or technology differentiation would sharpen this range.",
