      "narrative": "Teradar is a Series B defense and security technology company that has raised $175M to date. The target operates within a competitive landscape of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public and 8 private\u2014spanning the defense and security sector at matching development stages. Peer companies include Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $332M. Peer-median analysis across the 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a $1.0B implied valuation, with peer range spanning $300M to $3.0B. These methods bracket a wide but defensible outcome space.\n\nTriangulation of both methods supports a valuation range of $283M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $666M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Teradar's positioning within the peer cohort. Key drivers of variance include the company's competitive differentiation relative to better-capitalized peers, path to revenue commercialization, and whether Defense & Security sector multiples will sustain at current levels. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively; peer-median reflects market pricing but exhibits high dispersion. Additional commercial milestones and customer traction would narrow this range materially.",
