      "narrative": "Lux Aeterna is a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Brian Taylor, formerly of SpaceX Starlink, Amazon Project Kuiper, and Loft Orbital. The company has raised $14M to date. The Space & Aerospace sector comprises 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs, though no private peers share identical stage and valuation characteristics.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the sole applicable method. Using total raised ($14M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical Seed-to-next-stage multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $35M. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of disclosed revenue. Peer-median analysis is inapplicable; while 14 same-sector companies exist, zero meet narrow filters for same-stage, adjacent-stage, and valuation-tier proximity, and sector-wide median multiples would introduce material distortion.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $30M (low) to $40M (high), with $35M as the median point. This range reflects reliance on a single method and founder pedigree, creating concentrated analytical risk. Key uncertainties include undisclosed revenue trajectory, competitive positioning within the crowded launch-services ecosystem, and technical execution risk at the hardware stage. A revenue or customer anchor would materially sharpen the valuation bandwidth.",
