      "narrative": "Spaceium is a seed-stage space & aerospace company founded by Ashi Dissanayake and Reza Fetanat, both from the University of Ottawa with deep expertise in orbital mechanics, propulsion, and legacy engine systems. The company has raised $6.3M to date. The sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE.\n\nGiven Spaceium's stage and data constraints, the stage-progression method is the primary applicable approach. Using total capital raised ($6.3M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from seed to the next financing round yields $15.8M. Peer-median analysis could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the space sector\u2014while 14 sector peers exist, none met the threshold of three datapoints in tightly filtered cohorts. Public-comp anchoring using the sector P/S median of 27.4x is inapplicable absent target revenue disclosure, standard for private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $13M to $18M, with a median estimate of $16M. This range reflects methodological constraints rather than deep triangulation. Key uncertainties include the absence of near-peer seed financings in the space sector, undisclosed revenue or traction metrics that would unlock public-comp methods, and limited visibility into capital deployment and technical de-risking to date. A revenue-based approach or additional private-market comparables would materially strengthen conviction in any point estimate.",
