      "narrative": "Smack Technologies is a Series A\u2013stage Defense & Security company founded by Andy Markoff (former MARSOC and Palantir) and Clint Alanis (20+ years Marine special ops), having raised $32M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies: 2 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression uses the $32M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implying $64M. Peer-median triangulation examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Stark Defence at $4.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M, yielding a median of $400M. The wide range ($125M\u2013$4.0B) reflects significant heterogeneity within the peer cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $54M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $232M across both methods. The substantial gap between stage-progression ($64M) and peer-median ($400M) reflects tension between Smack's early funding history and the valuations commanded by comparable-stage defense-tech peers. Key uncertainties include revenue traction, customer concentration, and product differentiation relative to the peer set, particularly against the outlier valuation of Stark Defence at $4.0B.",
