      "narrative": "PAVE Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Julie B\u00f6hning and J\u00e9r\u00e9my Marciacq, both alumni of the Gruy\u00e8re Space Program at EPFL. The company has raised $40M to date. The valuation universe includes five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nStage-progression analysis provides the primary quantitative anchor. Applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier from seed to the next financing stage yields an implied valuation of $100M. This method is applicable given the company's clear stage positioning and established capital raise to date. Peer-median valuation proved inapplicable: while 14 same-sector peers exist, none satisfied the filters for sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables (threshold: \u22653 datapoints). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples was also inapplicable; the Space & Aerospace public median stands at 27.4x across the five tickers identified, but PAVE Space's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $85M to $115M, with a median of $100M. Material uncertainties remain around revenue trajectory and capital efficiency relative to stage peers. The single-method foundation limits confidence; future rounds incorporating disclosed revenue or additional private-market transactions would strengthen triangulation.",
