      "narrative": "Phoenix Tailings, a Series B climate and energy company that has raised $117.8M to date, is valued within a comp universe spanning one public company (LNZA) and eight private peers in the frontier energy technology sector, including later-stage contemporaries KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, which uses total capital raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $224M. Peer-median analysis across the three closest comparables\u2014all Series C stage in climate and energy\u2014produces a $1.0B midpoint valuation, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. The peer median method carries higher weight given the availability of direct sector and stage comparables.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $190M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $612M. The wide spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around execution risk and capital efficiency relative to later-stage peers. KoBold's $3.0B valuation and Amogy's $700M represent material endpoints within the peer set. Key sensitivities include demonstration of technical viability, pathway to capital efficiency post-Series B, and whether Phoenix Tailings' specific tailings remediation approach commands technology risk premium or discount relative to broader energy transition peers.",
