      "narrative": "Shield AI, a Series G defense and security company, commands a current post-money valuation of $12.7B following $1.5B+ in total fundraising. The valuation analysis triangulates against a comparable universe of 10 peers: two public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and eight private firms spanning Seed through Series H, including Anduril Industries ($61.0B), Helsing ($18.0B), Saronic ($9.2B), and Flock Safety ($7.5B).\n\nTwo methodologies anchor this analysis. Stage-progression, applying a 1.25x step-up multiplier typical for Series G advancement to the $5.6B last post-money valuation, implies $7.0B. Peer-median valuation across the nine same-sector, similar-tier comparables yields $7.5B, with a range spanning $3.0B to $61.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in defense tech business models and maturity, though the interquartile concentration suggests normalized pricing at the $7.0B\u2013$7.5B band.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $6.0B (low) to $8.6B (high), with a median of $7.2B. The current $12.7B valuation sits materially above this derived range, reflecting either market expectations for accelerated growth, strategic scarcity premium, or potential overvaluation relative to observable peer metrics. Key uncertainties include revenue multiples for early-stage defense contractors, customer concentration risk, and regulatory tailwinds or headwinds affecting sector-wide valuations.",
