      "narrative": "Castelion, a Series B defense and security company founded by Bryon Hargis, Sean Pitt, and Andrew Kreitz, is evaluated against a universe of 10 comparable companies: 2 public peers (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms in the same sector and stage. The company currently carries a $1.0B post-money valuation following $100M in total capital raised.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a 1.9x multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $1.9B. Peer-median benchmarking across six same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Defense Unicorns ($1.0B), Heven AeroTech ($1.0B), and one additional peer\u2014yielded a median of $1.1B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $956M (low) to $2.2B (high), with a median of $1.5B. Castelion's current $1.0B valuation sits at the lower bound of this range, near the peer median. Key uncertainties include the dispersion within the peer set (three-fold range) and the stage-progression multiplier assumption, which may not fully account for company-specific growth trajectory or market positioning within the defense sector.",
