      "narrative": "Kairos Power, a late-stage nuclear energy company founded by Mike Laufer, Edward Blandford, and Per Peterson, has raised over $500M and operates within a sector containing 3 public comparables (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 6 private peers including Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nThe valuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, as peer-median triangulation proved inapplicable due to insufficient narrow-stage comparables in nuclear energy. While 5 same-sector peers exist, none satisfied filters for matching stage, adjacent stage, or valuation tier simultaneously\u2014a data constraint that precludes reliable multiples-based benchmarking. The stage-progression method applies a 1.2x step-up multiplier to the $500M total raised proxy, yielding an implied valuation of $600M.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $510M to $690M, centered at $600M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single applicable method rather than triangulation across multiple independent approaches. The primary uncertainties are: (1) the absence of comparable late-stage nuclear energy private companies with disclosed valuations, limiting peer validation; and (2) the choice of multiplier sensitivity\u2014the 1.2x assumption moderates but does not eliminate methodological constraint. Further refinement would require either disclosed valuations from peer funding rounds or adjusted public-market comps with explicit nuclear-sector risk adjustments.",
