      "narrative": "Reflect Orbital is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Ben Nowack and Tristan Semmelhack, having raised $35.2M to date. The sector contains a modest peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only stage-progression analysis was applicable. Using $35.2M in total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $70.4M. Peer-median analysis could not be executed due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum dataset requirements (0 same-stage peers identified). Public-comp anchoring was not feasible in the absence of disclosed revenue figures, despite a 27.4x median price-to-sales multiple across the 5 public Space & Aerospace comps.\n\nThe single-method result constrains confidence in the valuation range. Stage-progression analysis supports a central estimate of $70M, with a range of $60M (low) to $81M (high) reflecting typical variance around the 2.0x multiplier. The primary valuation uncertainty stems from the absence of revenue disclosure and inability to cross-validate via peer multiples or public-market anchoring. Additional resolution would require comparable Series A or Series B funding rounds in adjacent space-infrastructure verticals.",
