      "narrative": "Etched is a Series E chip design company currently valued at $5.0B post-money, having raised $800M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a comparable universe of 8 private peers in Chips & Semiconductors (SambaNova Systems at $11.0B, PsiQuantum at $7.0B, Tenstorrent at $2.7B, Rebellions at $2.3B, and Ouster at $2.3B) and 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-Progression analysis applies a 1.4x step-up multiplier typical of Series E advancement to the $5.0B base valuation, implying $7.0B. Peer-Median analysis across the 8 same-sector comparables yields a median of $2.3B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $11.0B. Public-Comp Anchoring is not applicable given the absence of disclosed revenue data. The wide dispersion in peer valuations reflects heterogeneous stage maturity and market positioning within the sector.\n\nThe two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $2.0B to $8.0B, with a median implied value of $4.7B. Etched's current $5.0B valuation sits near this midpoint but slightly above the peer median, reflecting its advanced Series E stage relative to the broader cohort. Key uncertainties include the target's path-to-revenue timing, technical differentiation relative to peers, and sector macro conditions affecting frontier chip development valuations.",
