      "narrative": "Cuby Technologies is a Series B-stage company in Housing & Construction that has raised $23.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of four private comparables (Plantd Materials, Cover, Somos, and Charge Robotics), with no direct public trading comps available in this frontier subsector.\n\nA stage-progression methodology was applied, using the $23.4M total raised as a proxy for enterprise value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement. This approach yielded an implied valuation of $44M. Given limited methodological diversity due to data constraints, the analysis establishes a range of $38M (low) to $51M (high), with a median estimate of $44M.\n\nThe single-method triangulation reflects meaningful uncertainty. Key sensitivities include the appropriateness of the 1.9x multiplier for Housing & Construction specifically, comparability of the four private peers to Cuby's technology stage and market position, and the absence of public benchmarks for calibration. The median estimate of $44M should be interpreted as a directional anchor rather than a precise valuation, pending either expanded comp availability or additional methodologies such as venture capital method analysis tied to specific revenue or unit economics milestones.",
