      "narrative": "Forterra is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Alberto Lacaze that has raised $228M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers operating in the same sector and stage. Primary comparables include Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the company's $228M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a valuation of $433M. Peer-median analysis across the 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $300M (floor) to $3.0B (ceiling). The peer set exhibits substantial dispersion, reflecting heterogeneity in capital intensity and market position within the defense tech space.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $368M (low), $717M (median), and $1.1B (high). This 3x spread reflects meaningful uncertainty around Forterra's positioning relative to higher-capitalized peers like Dream Security and more modestly valued peers near the $300M threshold. Key variables driving outcomes include technology differentiation, customer concentration, and path to Series C funding timelines.",
