      "narrative": "SkySafe, a Series B defense and security company founded by Grant Jordan, is valued against a peer set of 10 comparable companies: 2 public-market comps (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns. The company has raised $50M+ to date.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate to a range. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $95M based on the $50M total raised proxy. The peer-median approach references 7 same-sector, same-stage comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B and a range of $300M\u2013$3.0B, reflecting material dispersion in the defense tech space. The two methods produce substantially different signals, reflecting both the early-stage nature of the company and heterogeneity within the peer cohort.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $81M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $548M. The wide spread reflects a key uncertainty: whether SkySafe's operational traction and market position align with the lower (stage-progression) or upper-quartile peer cohort. Further diligence on revenue run rate, customer concentration, and competitive differentiation is required to narrow this range meaningfully.",
