      "narrative": "Darkhive is a Series A-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $22M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable set spanning 10 private and 2 public peers operating in the same sector, including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $22M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage advancement, implying a $44M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a $400M implied valuation. The peer sample spans a wide range from $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence), with a median of $400M.\n\nSynthesizing these methods produces a triangulated range of $37M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $222M. The wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity within the Defense & Security peer set at Series A stage. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively on capital deployed; the peer-median approach captures market pricing but is sensitive to the composition of the comparison set, particularly the influence of higher-valued outliers. Key uncertainties include the appropriate peer weighting given the $4.0B-to-$125M spread, the company's specific technology differentiation relative to named comparables, and customer traction metrics not provided in this analysis.",
