      "narrative": "Deterrence is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $10M+ to date. The peer universe comprises four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables spanning Seed and Series A funding rounds, anchored by UFORCE ($1.0B), Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M). The broader Defense & Security ecosystem includes 10 evaluated peers (2 public, 8 private).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy, applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage transitions, yielding $25M. Peer-Median analysis across the four comparables produces $700M, reflecting the median of a $125M to $4.0B range. The dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven by heterogeneous commercial maturity and funding progress\u2014introduces meaningful range width.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $21M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $362M. The gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects the early-stage risk profile relative to more mature peers. Key uncertainties include Deterrence's product differentiation within the peer cohort, current burn rate and runway relative to the $10M+ raised, and near-term milestone achievement (revenue, customer traction, or technical validation). Closer inspection of the company's competitive positioning against UFORCE and other Seed-stage peers would refine placement within this range.",
