      "narrative": "Aalyria, a Series B space & aerospace company founded by Chris Taylor, has raised $130M+ and carries a last post-money valuation of $1.3B. The peer universe comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-stage companies including Rocket Lab, Sierra Space, and Cowboy Space Corporation.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $2.5B. Peer-median anchoring across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Skyryse at $1.1B) produces a $2.0B implied value. Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue disclosure. The public Space & Aerospace median trades at 27.4x revenue across 6 tickers, but this method remains inapplicable without Aalyria's top-line figures.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $1.7B to $2.8B, with a median of $2.2B. The current $1.3B post-money sits materially below this range, suggesting upside in any Series C fundraise. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion within the peer set ($1.1B to $8.0B) and reliance on two methods rather than three. Revenue disclosure would enable public-comp validation and narrow the range substantially.",
