      "narrative": "Re:Build Manufacturing, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Miles Arnone, Jeff Wilke, Anthony Manzo, and Michael Foley, has raised $545M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private and one public company in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including peers such as Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Walden Robotics across Series Seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $545M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $1.1B. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $926M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.4B. Key uncertainties include the stage heterogeneity within the peer set (three Series B, one Seed) and the degree to which Re:Build's $545M raised to date reflects pre-Series A financing or includes Series A capital already deployed.",
