      "narrative": "Bedrock Energy is a Series A\u2013stage climate and energy company founded by Joselyn Lai, Silviu Livescu, and Joel Wishkovsky. The company has raised $15M+ to date. The comparable universe in Climate & Energy spans 9 private peers (including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen) and 1 public reference (Lonza, ticker LNZA), though narrow peer filtering by stage and valuation tier yielded insufficient datapoints for median-based triangulation.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable: stage-progression analysis. Using the $15M total raised as a value proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage advancement, this approach implies a post-money valuation of $30M. This method is grounded in observed cadence within frontier energy but relies on the assumption that Bedrock's capital trajectory and risk profile align with cohort norms.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $26M to $34M, centered at $30M. Key uncertainties include the absence of a robust narrow-peer dataset for validation and the inherent variability in stage-progression multiples across capital efficiency and market conditions. Investors should treat this range as illustrative pending deeper diligence into unit economics, IP defensibility, and customer traction.",
