      "narrative": "Manna Aero is a Series B drone and autonomous systems company that has raised $110M to date. The comparable universe in Drones & Autonomous includes 8 private peers (Elroy Air, Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and others) with no public comps available. The narrow peer set\u2014same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier private companies\u2014lacks sufficient density (fewer than 3 datapoints) to support a reliable peer-median valuation.\n\nGiven data constraints, the Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable approach. This method applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $110M total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation, yielding an implied value of $209M. This multiplier reflects typical step-up dynamics from Series B onward. The method is grounded in the observable pattern that valuations advance 1.9x between intermediate stages in venture progression, though it does not incorporate company-specific performance metrics or market conditions.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $178M to $240M, with a midpoint of $209M. The range reflects conservative and optimistic applications of the stage-progression framework. Key uncertainties include the absence of narrow-set peer comparables, which limits validation of the derived range, and the lack of performance data (revenue, growth rate, unit economics) specific to Manna Aero. Any revision should incorporate recent financial performance or revised peer benchmarks.",
