      "narrative": "Primer AI is a Series D-stage defense and security software company that has raised $237M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers in the same sector and stage, including Helsing, Saronic, Chaos Industries, Onebrief, and Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo quantitative methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses the $237M total capital raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 1.5x multiplier typical of Series D-to-subsequent-stage step-ups, yielding $356M. The peer-median method examines four directly comparable Series D companies in Defense & Security, which span a wide range from $2.1B (Onebrief) to $18.0B (Helsing), with a median of $6.9B. This dispersion reflects material variation in market positioning, customer concentration, and revenue scale within the frontier-defense software cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $302M (low) to $7.9B (high), with a median of $3.6B. The extreme width of this range\u2014spanning more than 26x\u2014reflects genuine uncertainty about Primer's positioning relative to both the capital-raised baseline and the heterogeneous peer set. Key sensitivities include revenue traction relative to peer benchmarks, customer concentration risk, and the degree to which defense-sector regulatory tailwinds are priced into comparable valuations.",
