      "narrative": "Theseus is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Stanford and McGill-trained engineers, having raised $4.3M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public firms operating in defense technology, including peers at Seed and Series A stages such as UFORCE ($1.0B), Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression, using total raised as a proxy base and applying a typical 2.5x multiplier from Seed to next stage, implies a valuation of $11M. Peer-Median analysis across four same-sector comparables yielded a median valuation of $700M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in stage and maturity within the defense tech peer set.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $9M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $355M. The 89x spread between low and high estimates reflects material uncertainty. The Stage-Progression method yields results at the range floor and likely understates value given Theseus's technical team composition and the sector's current capital intensity. The Peer-Median approach is more representative but is sensitive to peer selection and stage alignment. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and how defensible the company's technical approach proves relative to better-capitalized incumbents.",
