      "narrative": "Zap Energy is a Series D nuclear energy company that has raised $330M+ to date. The valuation landscape for frontier nuclear comprises 3 public peers (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 6 private comparables including Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy. However, comparable-company analysis proves constrained: no private nuclear peers share Zap's stage, valuation tier, and development profile simultaneously, falling short of the minimum three-datapoint threshold for reliable peer medians.\n\nConsequently, stage-progression methodology dominates the triangulation. Using $330M in total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement yields $495M. This single-method approach generates a point estimate rather than a range anchored by multiple independent techniques. A sensitivity band around this figure\u2014accounting for variance in stage-specific multipliers and market conditions\u2014suggests a plausible range of $421M to $569M.\n\nThe median implied valuation of $495M rests primarily on stage-based trajectory rather than peer cross-validation. Key uncertainties include the absence of proven comparable exits in the ultra-early nuclear segment, the nascent nature of frontier fission commercialization timelines, and sensitivity to cost-of-capital assumptions across a sector with material regulatory and technical risk.",
