      "narrative": "Proteus Space is a Series A-stage company in the Space & Aerospace sector that has raised $14.4M to date. The company is led by CEO David Kervin, who brings 20+ years of government contract execution experience and military background, alongside CTO Andrew Shapiro, whose 20-year tenure at NASA JPL included managing technology formulation and 3D-printed component development for the Mars Perseverance Rover. The broader Space & Aerospace sector includes five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total raised ($14.4M) as a valuation proxy of $17M and applying a standard 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression to the next financing stage yields $34M. Peer-median analysis could not proceed due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within a narrow quality band\u2014only two adjacent-stage peers were identified among 14 sector companies. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 27.4x across the five tickers) was not feasible absent the target's revenue disclosure, which remains unavailable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $29M\u2013$39M, centered on $34M. This estimate carries material uncertainty given reliance on a single method and absence of revenue-based anchoring. Validation through future fundraising outcomes and revenue trajectory will be essential to test the stage-progression assumption.",
