      "narrative": "Ursa Major Technologies is a Series E-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $85M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 5 public-market peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-stage companies including ICEYE, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $85M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.4x multiplier typical of Series E advancement, yields $119M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (ICEYE at $12.0B, Apex Space at $2.3B, Varda at $1.6B) produces a median valuation of $2.3B, with a range spanning $1.6B to $12.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied; the sector median of 27.4x across six public tickers is calculable, but Ursa Major's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a wide triangulated range of $101M to $2.6B, with a median of $1.2B. The divergence reflects stage and growth-trajectory heterogeneity within the peer set. Key uncertainties include the company's actual revenue run-rate, customer concentration, and technical differentiation versus ICEYE and other incumbents. A Series E financing would more credibly anchor valuation; absent that, the $1.2B\u2013$2.3B band warrants consideration pending revenue visibility.",
