      "narrative": "Destinus is a late-stage defense and security company that has raised over $400M to date. The valuation universe comprises 10 private peers (including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI) and 2 public comparables (DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS), though the private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or similar-tier clustering to support reliable median multiples.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology was the primary applicable approach. Using the $400M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.2x multiplier typical for late-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $480M. This method reflects incremental value accretion beyond capital deployed but does not incorporate revenue or profitability multiples, limiting its precision. Peer-median analysis was not viable; while 23 defense and security peers exist in the broader sector, filtering for stage and valuation tier produced fewer than three datapoints, making comparative multiples unreliable.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $408M to $552M, with a median of $480M. This range reflects a \u00b115% confidence band around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the company's actual revenue and margin profile relative to public defense contractors, the degree of technological differentiation versus adjacent-stage peers, and broader defense budget and procurement cycle dynamics. A narrower range would require either disclosed financial metrics or a denser peer set at equivalent maturity and valuation tiers.",
