      "narrative": "Terran Robotics is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Zach Dwiel and Danny Weddle. The target operates within a broader sector comprising 9 private peers (including Walden Robotics, Divergent, and Exotec) and 1 public comparable. The company has raised $256K to date.\n\nOur valuation methodology relies on stage-progression analysis, the only applicable triangulation method given data constraints. We applied a 2.5x step-up multiplier to the $256K raised proxy, reflecting typical progression from Seed to next-stage financing. This yielded an implied valuation of $640K. The peer-median approach was not viable; while 10 same-sector robotics companies exist in the comp universe, narrow filtering by stage, timing, and valuation tier yielded fewer than 3 datapoints, making median extrapolation unreliable.\n\nOur analysis supports a valuation range of $544K to $736K, centered on $640K. The range reflects downside and upside sensitivity around the single applicable method. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 2.5x multiplier for this specific stage transition, the company's differentiation relative to the identified peer set, and the limited transaction data available at the Seed stage in robotics. Further validation would require additional Seed-stage comparables or direct revenue/metrics data from Terran Robotics itself.",
