      "narrative": "Insitro is a Series C-stage biotech company founded by Daphne Koller that has raised $1.1B+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private biotech and health companies at similar stages, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $1.1B total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implying a $1.9B valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range spanning $3.1B (New Limit) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences). Public comp anchoring via sector P/S multiples (6.2x median across the three public tickers) cannot be applied, as Insitro's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $1.6B (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.8B. The wide dispersion\u2014particularly the $10.3B outlier in the peer set\u2014reflects heterogeneity in biotech valuations at this stage. Key uncertainties include Insitro's revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and stage-progression timing to Series D or later financing rounds.",
