      "narrative": "Eikon Therapeutics, a Series B biotech company founded by Luke Lavis, Eric Betzig, Robert Tjian, and Xavier Darzacq, carries a current post-money valuation of $539M against $1.1B+ raised. The valuation universe comprises 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers, with immediate stage-adjacent reference points including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $539M base, implying $1.0B at the next funding stage. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, adjacent-stage comparables yields a $3.8B median (range: $3.1B\u2013$10.3B). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (6.2x median across the sector) cannot be applied, as private company revenue is not disclosed. These two methods triangulate to a low of $870M, median of $2.4B, and high of $4.4B.\n\nThe $2.4B median estimate sits substantially above current post-money but below the upper peer quartile. Key uncertainties include revenue traction (undisclosed), clinical-stage progression risk, and the wide dispersion within peer valuations ($3.1B\u2013$10.3B), which reflects heterogeneous risk profiles across the biotech cohort.",
