      "narrative": "Nuro, a Series G autonomous delivery drone company founded by Dave Ferguson and Jiajun Zhu, is evaluated against a comp universe of four private-stage peers in the Drones & Autonomous sector, including Zipline (Series G, $7.6B), Joby Aviation (Public, $6.9B), Archer Aviation (Public, $3.3B), and Elroy Air. The target's last post-money valuation stands at $6.0B against $2.2B total capital raised.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a typical 1.25x multiplier for Series G advancement, yields $7.5B. Peer-median analysis across three comparable companies\u2014filtered for sector and valuation tier\u2014produces $6.9B, with a range spanning $3.3B to $7.6B. The peer-median approach reflects meaningful dispersion in the autonomous vehicle space, reflecting execution risk variation across the cohort.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $5.8B (low) to $8.6B (high), with a median of $7.2B. The current $6.0B valuation sits below the median implied value, suggesting moderate upside to the $7.2B midpoint. Key uncertainties include regulatory pathway clarity for autonomous last-mile delivery, near-term path to positive unit economics, and competitive intensity within the sector\u2014all of which explain the $5.3B spread between low and high estimates.",
