      "narrative": "PsiQuantum, a private-stage semiconductor company founded by Jeremy O'Brien, Terry Rudolph, Peter Shadbolt, and Mark Thompson, is currently valued at $7.0B after raising $1.0B. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 11 total peers in Chips & Semiconductors\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private entities including SambaNova Systems, Etched, Tenstorrent, Rebellions, and Ouster.\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach. Across 6 same-sector peers with similar valuation profiles, the median valuation stands at $2.5B, with a range spanning $2.0B (Tenstorrent, Rebellions, Ouster) to $11.0B (SambaNova Systems). Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples cannot be applied because PsiQuantum's revenue is not disclosed; public Semiconductors peers trade at a median 21.0x price-to-sales, but this requires revenue data. The peer-median method implies a valuation of $2.5B.\n\nThe triangulated range supports $2.1B to $2.9B (median $2.5B), representing a substantial gap versus the current $7.0B valuation. The analysis is constrained by a single applicable method and the absence of revenue disclosure for private-company comparables. Key uncertainties include the target's growth trajectory, capital efficiency relative to peers, and technology differentiation in quantum computing infrastructure, which remain unquantified in this dataset.",
