      "narrative": "FleetZero is a Series A transportation company founded by Steven Henderson and Mike Carter that has raised $43M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 8 private companies in the transportation sector, including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Pipedream, and REGENT Craft; no public transportation comparables were available for direct benchmarking.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable valuation technique. Using FleetZero's $43M total raised as a baseline proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-Series B transitions, this method implies a valuation of $86M. A peer-median approach could not be reliably applied given insufficient narrow-filter matches within the same stage and adjacent valuation tiers\u2014only 3 total sector peers exist, and none met the minimum three-datapoint threshold for the same or adjacent stage.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $73M (low) to $99M (high), with a median of $86M. This relatively tight band reflects reliance on a single validated method. Key uncertainties include the applicability of standard step-up multipliers in frontier transportation, where market dynamics and capital intensity differ materially from conventional software or services comps. A broader private peer dataset at comparable stages would strengthen confidence in the range.",
