      "narrative": "Fortastra is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Mike Smayda that has raised $8M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers including Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C), alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised ($8M) as a proxy for enterprise value and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, yields $142M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 comparable companies produces $1.6B, with the range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of revenue disclosure, though the sector median P/S multiple stands at 27.4x across the public set.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $121M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $896M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Fortastra's revenue trajectory, technology differentiation, and market positioning relative to peers. Stage-progression generates a conservative bound; peer medians suggest substantially higher value if Fortastra approaches comparable scale. Resolution of revenue and near-term growth visibility would meaningfully narrow this range.",
