      "narrative": "Newcleo is a Series B nuclear energy company founded by Stefano Buono, Luciano Cinotti, and Elisabeth Rizzotti, having raised $755M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers across the nuclear energy sector\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised of $755M as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement yields an implied post-money valuation of $1.4B. This method reflects observed capital efficiency patterns at comparable funding stages within the nuclear sector.\n\nPeer-median comparison cannot be reliably applied; while five peers exist in the nuclear energy space, the narrow filters for same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar-valuation-tier peers yield insufficient datapoints (fewer than three required for statistical confidence). A broader peer-set median would risk introducing sector-wide noise unrepresentative of Newcleo's specific stage and positioning.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.2B to $1.6B, with a median of $1.4B. Key uncertainties center on technology de-risking timelines, regulatory pathway clarity for advanced reactor designs, and the timing of revenue inflection. The single-method reliance reflects data constraints; validation would strengthen with additional same-stage private nuclear comparables or disclosed recent funding rounds.",
