      "narrative": "Oxford Nanopore Technologies is a public-stage biotech company in the Biotech & Health sector. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set of 3 public peers in the same sector and stage: Recursion Pharmaceuticals ($1.6B), Freenome ($1.1B), and Alto Neuroscience ($1.0B). An additional 8 private frontier-biotech companies were identified but not formally included in quantitative triangulation.\n\nPeer-Median valuation, the sole applicable method given the absence of disclosed revenue, yields $1.1B. This median reflects the central tendency across the 3-company peer set, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. Public-Comp Anchoring using sector price-to-sales multiples (median 6.2x across Biotech & Health tickers RXRX, TEM, and ONT.L) cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not on file.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $935M to $1.3B, with a median of $1.1B. This relatively tight band reflects reliance on a single method and peer homogeneity. Key uncertainties include: the limited peer sample (n=3), which magnifies sensitivity to individual outliers; lack of revenue visibility for revenue-multiple cross-checks; and stage-specific factors (public biotech volatility, pipeline risk) that peer comparables may not fully capture. Investors should weight this analysis as a single anchor point rather than a definitive valuation.",
