      "narrative": "Renaissance Fusion is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Francesco Volpe and Martin Kupp that has raised $60.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 peers across public and private markets: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Valar Atomics, Fuse Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, Oklo, and X-Energy, spanning Seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using total capital raised as a valuation proxy, applies a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, yielding $121M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014produces a median of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects stage and technology maturity differences within nuclear energy.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $103M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $464M. Key uncertainties include the applicability of significantly more mature comparables like Valar Atomics at later stage, and the relative technical and commercialization risk positioning of Renaissance Fusion within its peer cohort. Stage-progression anchors conservatively; peer median reflects wider market activity but with substantial variance.",
