      "narrative": "Verkor, a Series C climate and energy company, has raised \u20ac3B+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on two primary methods triangulated against a peer set of three same-stage, same-sector private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M) and one public comparable (LNZA).\n\nThe Stage-Progression method applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $3.0B raised proxy, yielding $5.1B. The Peer-Median method anchors to the median valuation of three direct comparables at $1.0B, though this peer set exhibits wide dispersion ($700M to $3.0B). These two methods produce a 5.1x divergence, reflecting material heterogeneity in how Series C climate-tech companies are valued at present.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a range of $850M (low) to $5.9B (high), with a median of $3.0B. The wide range reflects two sources of uncertainty: first, the sparse peer set (n=3) limits statistical confidence; second, stage-progression multiples in frontier-tech sectors remain inconsistently applied. The $3.0B median is driven substantially by the highest-valued peer (KoBold) and the stage-based methodology, while the peer-median alone suggests meaningful downside. Resolution of valuation hinges on capital deployment trajectory and market reception of commercialization milestones.",
