      "narrative": "Neko Health is a Series C-stage biotech and health company founded by Daniel Ek and Hjalmar Nilsonne, having raised $326M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public biotech peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage companies in the same sector, with particular attention to 3 directly comparable Series C biotech firms: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to the $700M total-raised proxy and applying a 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, yields $1.2B. Peer-median valuation across the three same-stage, same-sector comparables produces $3.8B, with a range of $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring using the sector's 6.2x price-to-sales median cannot be applied, as target revenue is not disclosed. These two methods triangulate to a median valuation of $2.5B, bounded by a low of $1.0B and high of $4.4B.\n\nThe wide spread between methods\u2014driven principally by the $7.2B range within the peer set itself\u2014reflects material uncertainty around comparable company selection and stage-specific risk adjustment. The stage-progression floor and peer median represent the most defensible anchors given available data.",
