      "narrative": "ANYbotics is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 3 same-stage private comparables in Robotics & Manufacturing (Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity), supplemented by a broader universe of 8 private peers and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of $95M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range from $1.6B (Dexterity) to $2.0B (Generalist AI). The wide dispersion reflects genuine variance in market valuations within the robotics sector at this stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low estimate of $81M, a median of $922M, and a high of $2.0B. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects asymmetric information: the peer cohort likely incorporates proprietary revenue, customer concentration, and IP strength not captured by capital-raised metrics alone. Key uncertainties include whether ANYbotics' technology differentiation and commercial traction align with higher-valued peers like Generalist AI, or whether it tracks closer to lower-valued robotics entrants. Revenue data and customer diversity would materially narrow this range.",
