      "narrative": "Ramon.Space is a Series B space & aerospace company that has raised $43.5M to date. The valuation analysis applies two methodologies within a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space at $8.0B Series C, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B Series B, Aalyria at $1.3B Series B, and Skyryse at $1.1B Series C) and 5 public space & aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nStage-progression analysis uses the $43.5M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $83M. The peer-median method anchors to the median valuation of the 4 same-sector comparables at $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (27.4x median across the 5 public tickers) cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue data. These two applicable methods triangulate a valuation range of $70M to $1.9B, with a median of $866M.\n\nThe wide spread reflects material uncertainty in stage and competitive positioning within a nascent market. Stage-progression likely understates fair value given peer multiples; peer-median represents central tendency but carries dispersion risk given the $8.0B outlier. Revenue disclosure would enable public-comp validation and narrow the range materially.",
