      "narrative": "Mujin, a Series C-stage robotics and manufacturing automation company that has raised $85M+, is valued here against a peer universe of 9 private and 1 public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ). The three most relevant same-sector, same-stage peers are Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo valuation methods were triangulated. The stage-progression approach applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $85M raised proxy, implying $144M. The peer-median method draws on the three robotics comparables above, which exhibit a $1.0B\u2013$1.6B range with a median of $1.0B. This wide spread reflects variance in technology maturity, market traction, and capital efficiency within the cohort.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $123M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $572M. The 9x spread between low and high reflects material tension between bottom-up capital-based methods and peer-derived benchmarks. Key uncertainties driving this range include Mujin's current revenue and growth rate (not provided), customer concentration, and product-market fit relative to the peer set. A tighter range would require disclosure of recent revenue, ARR, or other operational milestones to anchor relative valuation multiples.",
