      "narrative": "Rapidus is a late-stage semiconductor company that has raised $5.0B+ to date. The valuation framework drew on a peer universe of 3 public semiconductors (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private frontier-chip competitors including Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nOf three triangulation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. The peer-median approach was inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow chip design segment\u201412 same-sector peers exist, but fewer than 3 met the stage and tier filters required for statistical reliability. Public-comp anchoring could not be executed because Rapidus, like most private companies, does not disclose revenue, precluding a price-to-sales multiple application to the 21.0x median observed across the three public semiconductor names.\n\nStage-progression analysis applied a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical of late-stage advancement, yielding $6.0B from the $5.0B raised proxy. This single-method result supports a median valuation of $6.0B, with a triangulated range of $5.1B (low) to $6.9B (high). Key uncertainties remain: the absence of disclosed financials limits precision; comparable late-stage chip ventures at similar funding levels are sparse; and the frontier-chip sector's rapid technical and competitive evolution creates material visibility risk beyond traditional stage-based progression.",
