      "narrative": "Innospace is a publicly listed Space & Aerospace company founded by Kim Soo-Jong, having raised $80M+. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of four same-sector, same-stage public comparables: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median approach is the applicable triangulation method here. The four-company median valuation is $5.2B, with a range spanning $840M at the low end to $40.0B at the high end. A public-comparable revenue multiple approach cannot be applied, as Innospace's revenue is not on file; the broader Space & Aerospace sector trades at a 27.4x P/S median across six public tickers, but this method requires disclosed revenue data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.4B to $6.0B, centered on the peer median of $5.2B. The primary uncertainty is the wide dispersion in the peer set itself\u2014the range from Astroscale to Rocket Lab spans nearly 48x\u2014reflecting material heterogeneity in company scale and market positioning within the public space sector. Revenue disclosure would enable triangulation via public multiples and would narrow confidence in the valuation range.",
