      "narrative": "Dronamics is a Series A drone logistics company operating in the Drones & Autonomous sector. The company has raised $43.2M to date. The relevant peer universe comprises 8 private companies in the sector, including Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air; no public comparables exist in this narrowly defined space.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable triangulation method, using total capital raised ($43.2M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A to subsequent-stage transitions. This yields an implied valuation of $86M. A sensitivity band around this central estimate\u2014accounting for variance in step-up magnitude and timing assumptions\u2014produces a low of $73M and a high of $99M.\n\nA peer-median approach cannot be reliably applied given insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum sample thresholds (fewer than 3 datapoints across filtered cohorts). Accordingly, the analysis relies on the single stage-progression result. The $73M\u2013$99M range, with $86M as the central estimate, reflects reasonable Series A positioning for Dronamics given capital deployed to date. Key uncertainties include the company's unit economics, customer traction, and the maturity and regulatory environment for autonomous cargo platforms, all of which would materially inform a refined estimate.",
