      "narrative": "Grain Weevil is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Chad and Ben Johnson that has raised $3.5M to date. The broader sector comprises one public company and eight private peers, including later-stage names such as Walden Robotics, Divergent, and Exotec, though a tight peer set at identical stage and valuation tier remains limited.\n\nOnly the stage-progression method proved applicable to this valuation. Using total capital raised ($3.5M, normalized to $4M) as a proxy for seed-stage value, a 2.5x step-up multiplier to the next funding round yields $9M. This multiplier reflects typical dilution and value-creation expectations for the seed-to-Series A transition in robotics-adjacent markets. Peer-median analysis could not be executed: while ten robotics and manufacturing peers exist in the broader dataset, the narrow filters (same stage, adjacent stage, similar valuation tier) returned insufficient observations\u2014fewer than the three-company minimum required for robust triangulation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $7M to $10M, with a median point of $9M. This single-method result carries material uncertainty. The range reflects 15% sensitivity around the base median, but lacks corroboration from comparable transactions. Key risks to valuation include the limited peer visibility at seed stage in this subsector and the dependency on stage-progression assumptions. A Series A fundraise or additional narrower peer data would substantially improve confidence in the estimate.",
