      "narrative": "Na\u00effo Technologies, a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Aymeric Barthes and Ga\u00ebtan S\u00e9v\u00e9rac, has raised \u20ac54.7M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 9 comparable companies\u20148 private firms and 1 public entity\u2014operating in the robotics and manufacturing sector at similar stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using total capital raised (\u20ac54.7M) as a proxy baseline, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, yielding \u20ac93M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Hadrian (\u20ac1.6B), Agile Robots (\u20ac1.0B), and Nimble Robotics (\u20ac1.0B). The median across these peers stands at \u20ac1.0B, with a range of \u20ac1.0B to \u20ac1.6B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a valuation range of \u20ac79M (low) to \u20ac1.1B (high), with a median of \u20ac546M. The substantial gap between stage-progression (\u20ac93M) and peer-median (\u20ac1.0B) reflects structural differences: the stage-progression method relies solely on historical capital deployed, while peer comparables incorporate market-based pricing for similar-stage robotics companies. Key uncertainties include whether Na\u00effo's technology, market position, and unit economics align with the higher-valued peer set or occupy a lower tier within the sector. Additional clarity on revenue, growth rates, and competitive differentiation would narrow this range materially.",
