      "narrative": "GrayMatter Robotics is a Series B-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $70M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 peers: 1 public company (277810.KQ) and 8 private firms including Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $300M last post-money valuation as a base and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying $570M. Peer-median analysis references three same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B)\u2014which yield a median valuation of $1.8B and a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nThese methods triangulate to a valuation range of $484M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.2B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around how robustly GrayMatter's stage-based progression compares to the peer set, which skews substantially higher. Key uncertainties include whether the company's growth trajectory and market position justify valuations nearer the peer median versus stage-based step-up, and whether recent funding activity or operational milestones would shift the base assumptions.",
