      "narrative": "Orbital Composites is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Cole Nielsen and Amolak Badesha that has raised $6.6M to date. The broader Robotics & Manufacturing sector includes one public comparable (277810.KQ) and eight private peers, including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. Using the $6.6M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.5x multiplier for progression from seed to next stage yields an implied valuation of $16.5M. This method reflects standard venture progression economics in the robotics sector. A peer-median approach could not be reliably applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the robotics manufacturing universe; while ten same-sector peers exist, fewer than three met narrow filtering criteria, making sector-wide median comparison uninformative.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $14M to $19M, with a median point of $16M. This range reflects \u00b115% bounds around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the precise composition of the $6.6M raise across tranches (which would refine the base proxy), the absence of tightly comparable seed-stage peers in robotics manufacturing, and the early-stage nature limiting hard financial or revenue metrics. The single-method foundation warrants validation against future fundraising or operational milestones.",
