      "narrative": "Chef Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Rajat Bhageria, is evaluated against a comparable universe of 1 public and 8 private firms in the sector, including Series B-stage peers Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B), alongside earlier-stage comparables like Walden Robotics ($1.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate the company's enterprise value. The stage-progression method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $15M proxy base derived from total capital raised of $65.6M, implying a $30M valuation. The peer-median approach yields $1.7B, anchored to the median valuation across the 4-company peer set with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The latter method reflects typical Series B robotics companies, introducing material stage-discount risk for a Series A asset.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $26M to $2.0B, with a median indication of $865M. The wide dispersion reflects the tension between stage-progression fundamentals and peer comparables skewed toward more mature companies. Key uncertainties include the appropriate stage-discount rate when peers predominantly occupy Series B, the timing and capital requirements for Chef Robotics' path to Series B, and normalized margins within hardware-robotics operations relative to the peer set.",
