      "narrative": "LeoLabs is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $94M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two applicable methodologies within a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, Skyryse) valued between $1.1B and $8.0B, alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $179M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the $1.6B median valuation across the four same-sector comparables, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp P/S anchoring (27.4x median across 6 tickers) cannot be applied without LeoLabs' revenue disclosure. These two applicable methods triangulate to a low of $152M, median of $914M, and high of $1.9B.\n\nThe wide spread between stage-progression ($179M) and peer-median ($1.6B) reflects meaningful uncertainty around whether LeoLabs' technology differentiation and market position align with the upper or lower quartile of the peer set. Stage-progression assumes modest expansion; peer median assumes competitive positioning closer to Cowboy or Aalyria. Revenue traction and customer concentration will be critical to resolving this range.",
