      "narrative": "Lumafield is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $142M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ), with primary focus on three same-stage, same-sector private peers: Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base of $10M and applying a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $17M. Peer-median analysis across the three robotics comparables yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. The peer-median method carries greater weight given its reliance on observable transaction data in the direct peer set.\n\nTriangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $14M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median indication of $508M. The extreme width of this range reflects material tension between the stage-progression method\u2014which penalizes reliance on capital raised as a valuation proxy\u2014and peer comparables, which suggest substantially higher values for robotics companies at this maturity stage. Key uncertainties include competitive differentiation relative to Hadrian and Agile Robots, Lumafield's revenue scale relative to peers, and market timing within the robotics sector.",
