      "narrative": "LanzaTech is a public-stage Climate & Energy company founded by Sean Simpson and Richard Forster, having raised over $500M to date. The valuation assessment relies on a peer-median methodology applied to a three-company comparable set within the same sector and stage: QuantumScape ($3.6B), Enovix ($1.0B), and Solid Power ($504M).\n\nThe peer-median method yields an implied valuation of $1.0B, representing the central tendency across the three public comparables. The peer range spans from $504M to $3.6B, establishing outer bounds for the analysis. Given the limited methodological depth available in the current dataset\u2014only one triangulation method is applicable\u2014this single approach carries correspondingly greater weight in the valuation. The median valuation of $1.0B aligns with Enovix's current public market valuation, suggesting LanzaTech occupies the middle ground within its peer cohort on a valuation basis.\n\nThe triangulated range supports a valuation of $850M to $1.1B, with $1.0B as the median estimate. This range reflects reasonable variation around the peer median but operates with material constraints: the analysis is supported by only one methodology, and the peer set itself spans a 7.2x range, indicating substantial heterogeneity in how the market values Climate & Energy companies at the public stage. Key uncertainties include profitability timing, capital efficiency relative to peers, and the representativeness of a three-company comparable set for a sector with limited public tradeable volume.",
