      "narrative": "Osmo, a Series B consumer tech company founded by Alex Wiltschko, has raised $130M to date. The valuation analysis is constrained by the absence of direct public comparables and identifiable private peer transactions in the available dataset, limiting triangulation to a single applicable methodology.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the primary valuation anchor, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $130M total capital raised as a proxy for Series B fair value. This yields an implied valuation of $247M. The methodology reflects typical Series B-to-later-stage advancement patterns, though its applicability depends on the assumption that capital raised reasonably approximates equity value at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $210M to $284M, with a median of $247M. This 35% band reflects reasonable variance around a single method rather than robust triangulation across independent approaches. The primary uncertainty stems from the absence of comparable transaction data\u2014neither public sector benchmarks nor private peer financing rounds are available to validate the stage-progression step-up. Investor conviction in this range should account for this methodological limitation and would benefit from additional market data on recent Series B consumer tech valuations or transaction comps within Osmo's specific subsector.",
