      "narrative": "Vivodyne is a Series A biotech & health company founded by Andrei Georgescu and Dan Huh, having raised $78M+ to date. The valuation exercise draws from a comp universe of 3 public biotech companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Recursion Pharmaceuticals, and Freenome, though direct peer multiples proved difficult to operationalize.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($78M) as a proxy for post-money value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $156M. The peer-median approach failed due to insufficient narrow peer density in the same stage and tier\u2014while 7 sector peers exist, none of the filtered subsets met the three-datapoint minimum for robust comparison. Public-comp anchoring using the 6.2x median P/S across the three public biotech comps was inapplicable because Vivodyne's revenue is not on file, a standard constraint for private company analysis.\n\nThe single-method result anchors valuation at $156M, with a triangulated range of $133M\u2013$179M reflecting method-inherent uncertainty rather than cross-method triangulation. The primary constraint is absence of revenue disclosure and limited comparable transaction data at Vivodyne's specific stage and technology focus. Refinement would benefit from either disclosed financials or transaction comps within the synthetic biology / computational biology subsegment.",
