      "narrative": "General Galactic, a Seed-stage Climate & Energy company founded by Halen Mattison and Luke Neise, has raised $10M to date. The comparable universe in Climate & Energy includes one public company (Lonza, ticker LNZA) and eight private peers, including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. However, a sufficiently tight peer set at the same stage and valuation tier does not exist to support a reliable peer-median approach\u2014only zero same-stage and zero adjacent-stage comparables met minimum clustering thresholds.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is applicable and forms the sole quantitative anchor for valuation. Using $10M in total raised as a base proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression yields $25M. This method assumes General Galactic will achieve comparable development and financing velocity to cohort peers advancing from Seed stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $21M to $29M, with a median of $25M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method and should be weighted accordingly. Key uncertainties include the applicability of a 2.5x stage multiplier to this specific company's trajectory, product maturity relative to sector peers, and capital deployment efficiency. Given the absence of tight-fit comparables, investors should conduct deep diligence on the company's technical differentiation and runway relative to sector benchmarks before commitment.",
