      "narrative": "Ares Industries is a Series A-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $31M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing\u2014all operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yields $62M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M)\u2014produces a median valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B. This wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in the peer set, with Stark Defence representing an outlier at the high end.\n\nTriangulation of both methods produces a valuation range of $53M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $231M. The 8.7x spread between low and high estimates reflects substantial uncertainty in comparable valuations and limited visibility into Ares' revenue, growth trajectory, and competitive positioning relative to the peer cohort. Refinement of this range would benefit from granular metrics on revenue multiples, customer concentration, and technology differentiation across the peer set.",
