      "narrative": "Fourth Power, a Series A climate and energy company founded by Asegun Henry and Arvin Ganesan, operates within a fragmented sector landscape comprising 1 public comparable (LNZA) and 8 private peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. The company has raised $40M+ to date.\n\nThe valuation analysis applies one triangulation method with sufficient rigor. Stage-progression modeling, anchored to the $40M total raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression to subsequent funding rounds, yielding an implied value of $80M. Peer-median analysis proved inapplicable: while 9 same-sector comparables exist in Climate & Energy, none returned three or more matches across tightened filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier), making median extraction statistically unreliable. A broad-sector median would introduce excessive noise.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $92M (high), with a median estimate of $80M. This narrow range reflects reliance on a single method and underscores material uncertainty around comparable company selection. Key risks to the valuation include stage-specific execution risk, absence of demonstrated traction metrics in the dataset, and the early-stage illiquidity discount inherent to Series A private deployment. Refinement would require additional same-stage or downstream-round data from the Climate & Energy peer set.",
