      "narrative": "Infleqtion, a public-stage quantum computing company founded by Dana Anderson, has raised $760M+ and currently trades at a $1.92B valuation. The quantum computing sector comprises a fragmented peer set of 11 comparable companies across public and private stages, including three public peers (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum) and eight private participants.\n\nThe peer-median method applied to four same-sector, same-stage public comparables yields an implied valuation of $5.4B. The comparable set ranges from $60M (Archer Materials) to $13.0B (IonQ), with D-Wave at $6.3B and Rigetti at $4.5B. This wide dispersion reflects heterogeneous market valuations across quantum approaches and commercialization timelines. The median of $5.4B implies a 2.8x uplift to Infleqtion's current trading level.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $4.6B to $6.2B (median $5.4B), though this analysis relies on a single applicable method given data constraints. The substantial gap between Infleqtion's current $1.92B valuation and the peer-median-derived range suggests either market undervaluation or differentiated risk perceptions relative to public comparables. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the peer sample given quantum computing's early-stage heterogeneity, the comparability of revenue models and paths to profitability, and broader sector sentiment shifts. Additional revenue multiple or DCF analysis would strengthen conviction in this range.",
