      "narrative": "Quantinuum, a Series G quantum computing company founded by Ilyas Khan, has raised $2.7B+ and carries a current post-money valuation of $14.8B. The quantum computing sector comp universe consists of three public peers (IonQ, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing) and five additional private participants, providing a reasonable basis for cross-sectional comparison.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to Quantinuum's $14.8B last post-money valuation and applying a typical Series G step-up multiplier of 1.25x, yields $18.5B. Peer-median analysis across the three public quantum computing comparables produces a median valuation of $6.3B, with a range spanning $4.5B (Rigetti Computing) to $13.0B (IonQ). The dispersion within this peer set reflects meaningful differences in technology approach and commercial maturity across the quantum sector.\n\nTriangulating these two methods implies a valuation range of $5.3B to $21.2B, with a median cross-check of $12.4B. The current $14.8B valuation sits above the peer median but within the stage-progression implied range, consistent with Quantinuum's later stage and capital raised to date. Key uncertainties center on quantum computing's path to commercial utility, the durability of current valuations in a sector with limited revenue contribution, and whether Quantinuum's technical approach commands a premium relative to public peer benchmarks.",
