      "narrative": "Nox Metals is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Zane Hengsperger that has raised $5.1M to date. The broader sector comprises nine private peers and one public comparable (277810.KQ), though narrow-stage filtering within Robotics & Manufacturing yielded insufficient datapoints for robust peer-median analysis.\n\nGiven sparse comparable availability at seed stage, stage-progression methodology was applied as the primary valuation lever. Using total raised ($5.1M) as a value proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement, this method implies a $13M valuation. The peer-median approach was deemed inapplicable: while the broader sector contains 10 robotics companies, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier peers returned fewer than three datapoints required for meaningful triangulation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $11M to $15M, with a median point of $13M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression result, accounting for execution risk at seed stage and the acknowledged scarcity of tightly comparable transactions. Key uncertainties include the lack of recent seed-stage comps in the robotics sector, the company's specific technology differentiation relative to named peers (Walden, Divergent, Exotec, Locus, Generalist AI), and near-term capital requirements that may influence follow-on round terms.",
