      "narrative": "Seurat Technologies is a Series C-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $178M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of nine private peers (Hadrian, Agile Robots, Nimble Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and others) and one public comparable, providing sector-relevant benchmarks for a maturing frontier-tech company.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method applies a 1.7x multiplier to total capital raised as a proxy baseline, implying a valuation of $303M. The peer-median approach anchors to three same-stage robotics companies: Hadrian at $1.6B, Agile Robots and Nimble Robotics each at $1.0B, yielding a median peer valuation of $1.0B. The peer range spans $1.0B to $1.6B, reflecting material variance within the cohort.\n\nSynthesizing these methods produces a triangulated valuation range of $257M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $651M. The substantial spread between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects a key uncertainty: whether Seurat's capital efficiency and market position align with the lower-quartile or median peer cohort. Absence of disclosed revenue or unit economics limits refinement of this range. Additional clarity on growth rates and customer concentration relative to the peer set would help narrow the valuation corridor.",
