      "narrative": "Aeva Technologies is a public-stage semiconductor company founded by Soroush Salehian and Mina Rezk, currently valued at $1.09B after raising $660M+. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 3 same-sector public peers (Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and Ouster) with valuations ranging from $2.3B to $39.2B.\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across the 3 public comparables in Chips & Semiconductors is $35.8B, derived from Cerebras at $39.2B, Credo Semiconductor at $35.8B, and Ouster at $2.3B. The public-comp anchoring method using price-to-sales multiples (sector median 21.0x) cannot be applied, as Aeva's revenue is not disclosed on file. Without revenue data, multiples-based valuation is not feasible.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $30.4B (low) to $41.2B (high), centered at $35.8B median. The wide spread ($2.3B to $39.2B) across the peer set reflects material heterogeneity in stage maturity and profitability within public semiconductor players. Key uncertainties include Aeva's actual revenue scale relative to peers, margin trajectory, and market share in its specific optical sensing subsegment. Only one valuation method is operable with available data, limiting triangulation robustness.",
