      "narrative": "Voyant Photonics is a Series A chip and semiconductor company that has raised $23M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a fragmented comp universe: three public semiconductor peers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) trade at a median 21.0x price-to-sales, while the private peer set includes eight companies such as SambaNova Systems, Cerebras, and Credo Semiconductor. However, meaningful cross-company triangulation is constrained by data limitations.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the primary applicable approach. Using total capital raised ($23M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression yields $46M. The public-comp anchoring method cannot be applied because Voyant's revenue is not disclosed; private companies rarely publish this metric, and without it, the 21.0x public median cannot be operationalized. The peer-median method also does not apply: while 12 same-sector peers exist, filtering for identical stage and valuation tier yields insufficient sample size (fewer than three comps required for reliable medians).\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $39M to $53M, centered at $46M. This range reflects the stage-progression output plus conservative bounds. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data (blocking public-comp methods), the thinness of same-stage private comparables, and the heterogeneity of the semiconductor subsectors represented in the peer set. Additional disclosure of unit economics or TAM would materially sharpen this estimate.",
