      "narrative": "Drafter is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Chris Barton and Peter Atkin, having raised $3M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 9 private robotics peers (including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI) and 1 public comparable (277810.KQ), though meaningful peer-stage alignment remains constrained.\n\nThe stage-progression method, the sole applicable triangulation approach, uses the $3M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the subsequent financing stage, yielding an implied valuation of $8M. This method is grounded in observable Seed-to-Series A advancement patterns but depends critically on Drafter's execution velocity and market conditions tracking historical norms.\n\nThe peer-median approach was not applied due to insufficient granularity: while 10 robotics peers exist sector-wide, fewer than three same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tiers were available, rendering a narrow peer median unreliable. This limitation suggests the broader robotics sector heterogeneity presents valuation risk.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6M to $9M, with a median point of $8M. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 2.5x multiplier to Drafter's specific risk profile and the absence of near-peer transaction data. Investors should weight execution on core robotics milestones as a primary driver of progression within this range.",
