      "narrative": "Amogy is a Series C climate and energy company founded by Seonghoon Woo that has raised $300M+ and carries a current post-money valuation of $700M. The peer universe consists of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014operating in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages. Key private peers include KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, Helion, Redwood Materials, and QuantumScape.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate on the company's fair value. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.7x multiplier to the $700M Series C post-money, implying a forward valuation of $1.2B. Peer-median analysis uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Redwood Materials at $6.0B (Series D), KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), and Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C). The median across these three peers is $3.0B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $6.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $1.0B (low) to $3.4B (high), with a median point of $2.1B. This implies meaningful upside from the current $700M valuation. Key uncertainties include stage-specific step-up assumptions and the wide dispersion in comparable valuations, which reflects variance in technology maturity, capital intensity, and market traction within the frontier energy sector.",
