      "narrative": "Simbe Robotics is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $100M+. The valuation assessment draws from a comp universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable across the sector, with primary focus on 3 same-stage private companies: Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression methodology uses the $100M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implying $170M. The peer-median approach benchmarks against the three same-sector, same-stage comparables, which exhibit a median valuation of $1.0B and a range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. This method directly implies $1.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide spread. Triangulation yields a low estimate of $144M, a median of $585M, and a high of $1.1B. The disparity reflects tension between the stage-progression anchor\u2014conservative relative to peer valuations\u2014and the peer-median floor at $1.0B. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to peers, revenue and growth trajectory relative to the Hadrian\u2013Nimble\u2013Agile cohort, and whether Simbe's market position and unit economics support peer-level multiples. The median estimate of $585M sits materially below peer valuations, suggesting either relative underperformance or that disclosed peers represent stronger franchises.",
