      "narrative": "Rugged Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Derrick J. Morse and Logan Farrell, having raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis incorporates a peer set of four robotics companies at Series A/B stages, complemented by a broader universe of 8 private peers and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply here. The stage-progression method, using the $12M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a valuation of $24M. The peer-median approach benchmarks against four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yielding a median valuation of $1.7B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThese methods produce a wide triangulated range of $20M to $2.0B, with a median of $862M. The substantial divergence reflects the acute stage and maturity gap between early Series A and the more advanced Series B cohort dominating the peer set. The $24M stage-progression result better reflects Series A market clearing, while the $1.7B median likely overstates fair value absent evidence of comparable revenue, unit economics, or deployment scale. Key uncertainties include the target's current revenue, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to named peers. A more refined estimate would require financials and operational metrics to bridge the valuation gap.",
