      "narrative": "Zeno Power is a Series B space & aerospace company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation assessment triangulates two applicable methods across a comp universe of 4 private peers in the same sector and stage: Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C).\n\nThe Stage-Progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $50M total raised proxy, implying a $95M valuation. The Peer-Median method anchors to the $1.6B median across the 4-company peer set, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public comp anchoring is not applicable; while 5 public Space & Aerospace tickers trade at a median P/S of 27.4x, Zeno Power's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $81M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $872M. This wide range reflects material uncertainty: the Stage-Progression method suggests substantially lower valuations relative to peer medians, while the peer set itself exhibits 7x dispersion ($1.1B\u2013$8.0B), driven partly by stage heterogeneity (two Series C comps) and likely differentiated technology maturity. The analysis is most sensitive to whether Zeno Power's technical standing and market position align with higher-quartile peers like Cowboy Space or lower-quartile peers like Aalyria.",
