      "narrative": "Evolv Technology is a publicly-traded Defense & Security company with a current market capitalization of $1.04B. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of 15 same-sector comparables spanning similar valuation tiers, comprising 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems.\n\nA peer-median approach was applied across the 15-company set, which spans valuations from $300M to $4.5B. The median valuation across this cohort is $1.4B, derived from peers at various stages\u2014ranging from Series A (Stark Defence at $4.0B) through Series F (Skydio at $4.4B). This method directly anchors to observed market pricing for comparable-stage, same-sector businesses and therefore carries substantial weight in the triangulation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.2B to $1.6B, with a median of $1.4B. Evolv's current $1.04B market cap sits below the peer median by approximately 26%, suggesting either a valuation discount relative to the cohort or positioning near the lower quartile of the Defense & Security peer set. The primary uncertainty stems from the single-method triangulation; additional valuation approaches (revenue multiples, DCF anchors, or transaction comparables) would strengthen conviction in the range and help isolate whether the discount reflects company-specific factors or broader market repricing.",
