      "narrative": "Akash Systems is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector peers at Series B and Series C stages, including Sierra Space ($8.0B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Aalyria ($1.3B), and Skyryse ($1.1B), alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables trading at a median P/S of 27.4x.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable given available data. The stage-progression approach applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement to the $40M raised proxy, implying a $76M valuation. The peer-median method anchors to the $1.6B median across the 4 same-sector comparables, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied, as target revenue is not disclosed\u2014a common limitation for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods yields a valuation range of $65M to $1.9B, with a median of $863M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around Akash's competitive positioning and revenue trajectory relative to peers. Stage-progression implies the lower bound, while peer-median dominates the midpoint and upper range. Without revenue data or visibility into product-market fit metrics, confidence narrows most defensibly to the $400M\u2013$1.2B band, anchored to lower-stage comparables within the peer set.",
