      "narrative": "Lilac Solutions, a Series C-stage climate and energy company, has raised $315M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two primary methods triangulated against a peer set of 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), supplemented by reference to a broader comp universe of 8 private and 1 public climate-tech firm.\n\nStage-progression methodology, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $536M based on total capital raised as a proxy. The peer-median approach yields $1.0B, reflecting the median across the three direct comparables with a range of $700M to $3.0B. The substantial spread reflects heterogeneity in the peer set\u2014KoBold's $3.0B valuation materially exceeds the cohort median, likely reflecting differences in technology maturity, capital intensity, or market positioning.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a range of $455M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $768M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound; peer-median analysis supports the upper bound. Key uncertainties include the relevance of KoBold and other peers given potential differences in technology risk, commercialization timeline, and addressable market scope. The wide $700M-$3.0B peer range underscores that sector comparables, while directionally useful, carry meaningful model sensitivity.",
