      "narrative": "Gravitics is a seed-stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised $20M in equity plus $60M in STRATFI financing. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 6 public Space & Aerospace peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private companies including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE.\n\nOf three candidate valuation methods, only stage-progression triangulation is applicable. The peer-median approach fails due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow aerospace subset\u2014while 14 same-sector peers exist, filtering for stage and tier yields fewer than the required 3 datapoints. Public-comp anchoring is inapplicable because Gravitics' revenue is not disclosed; the sector median P/S of 27.4x across public peers cannot be applied without this metric. Stage-progression uses the $20M equity raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression, implying a $50M valuation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $42M\u2013$57M, with a $50M median. This conclusion rests on a single methodological leg and carries material uncertainty. Key risks include: the absence of validated peer data for cross-check, reliance on capital raised rather than operational traction as a valuation anchor, and the illiquidity discount appropriate for seed-stage private equity. The $60M STRATFI component does not factor into traditional equity valuation without clarity on its terms.",
