      "narrative": "Lunar Outpost is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $23.6M to date. The valuation universe consists of 6 public-market comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and a broader private peer set including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs. The sector median revenue multiple across public comps stands at 27.4x.\n\nOnly one valuation method yielded sufficient data quality. Stage-progression analysis, using the $23.6M total raised as a valuation proxy, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression to the next financing stage, producing an implied valuation of $47M. Peer-median triangulation was not applicable\u2014while 14 same-sector peers exist, the narrow filters (same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar valuation-tier) returned fewer than three datapoints, making median-based inference unreliable. Public-comp anchoring via revenue multiples could not be executed because the target's revenue is not on file, a common data constraint for private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $40M to $54M, with a median of $47M. This range reflects upside/downside variance around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data (which would enable public-multiple anchoring), limited same-stage private comps, and reliance on a single method. Investors should treat this estimate as directional; deeper diligence on comparable financing rounds and revenue trajectory would strengthen conviction.",
