      "narrative": "MightyFly is a Series A-stage drone and autonomous vehicle company founded by Manal Habib that has raised $10M to date. The broader Drones & Autonomous sector comprises 8 private peers including Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air, with no public comparables available for direct benchmarking.\n\nThe valuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, as peer-median analysis proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow peer set. The stage-progression method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $10M total raised proxy, reflecting typical funding step-ups from Series A onward, yielding an implied valuation of $20M. This single-method approach constrains triangulation; however, sensitivity analysis around the step-up multiplier produces a range of $17M (low) to $23M (high) centered on the $20M median.\n\nThe $17M\u2013$23M range is defensible given the stage and capital deployed, though material uncertainty persists. Key limitations include the sparse peer set in the Drones & Autonomous sector at this stage, absence of public market anchors, and reliance on a single valuation method. Revenue, unit economics, and technology differentiation data were not available to calibrate the multiplier or test consistency with revenue-based or discounted-cash-flow approaches. The analysis would benefit from additional private comparables or revenue traction to narrow the range.",
