      "narrative": "Atomic AI is a Series A\u2013stage biotech company founded by Raphael Townshend that has raised $42M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private companies in the Biotech & Health sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, Recursion Pharmaceuticals, and Freenome.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. This method uses total capital raised ($42M) as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression to the next funding stage, yielding $84M. Peer-Median analysis could not be executed because the narrow peer set (same-stage or adjacent-stage companies within similar valuation tiers) contained fewer than the three datapoints required for statistical reliability. Public-Comp Anchoring, while supported by a median P/S of 6.2x across the three public biotech tickers, cannot be applied without the target's revenue figure, which remains undisclosed.\n\nThe triangulation range spans $71M to $97M, with a median point of $84M. This range reflects the bounds of uncertainty inherent in single-method valuation. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data, limited comparable peers at identical stage and scale, and reliance on a gross multiplier absent company-specific metrics. The analysis would benefit materially from disclosure of Atomic AI's revenue run rate or a richer set of closely comparable Series A biotech exits.",
