      "narrative": "Amber Bio is a seed-stage biotech company founded by Basem Al-Shayeb and Jacob Borrajo that has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public companies (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in Biotech & Health, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nGiven data constraints, only the Stage-Progression method is applicable. Using total capital raised ($26M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to the subsequent stage yields an implied valuation of $65M. The Peer-Median approach cannot be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum thresholds (fewer than 3 datapoints in narrow filters). Public-Comp Anchoring, while theoretically grounded on a Biotech & Health P/S median of 6.2x across the three public tickers, cannot be executed absent the target's revenue disclosure\u2014a common limitation in private company analysis.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $55M (low) to $75M (high), with a median point estimate of $65M. This range reflects modest sensitivity bounds around the single applicable method. The primary uncertainties are (1) the robustness of using total raised as a valuation proxy in a competitive seed environment and (2) the absence of granular peer financial data. Revenue disclosure would materially strengthen confidence in the valuation conclusion.",
