      "narrative": "Strand Therapeutics is a Series B biotech company founded by Jake Becraft, Tasuku Kitada, and Ron Weiss, having raised $205M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 8 private peers and 3 public comparables in Biotech & Health, including Series B and Series C stage companies such as Eikon Therapeutics ($539M), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression modeling applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $205M total raised proxy, implying a $390M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range from $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue for the target. The wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014driven by heterogeneous therapeutic approaches and development maturity\u2014limits precision of the peer method.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a range of $331M to $4.0B, with a median of $1.9B. The stage-progression floor reflects conservative sizing relative to raised capital; the peer ceiling reflects the upper quartile of Series C stage peers. Key uncertainties include the target's clinical stage advancement, intellectual property strength relative to peers, and management execution risk, which cannot be quantified from available data. The wide range warrants further diligence on pipeline specifics and comparative burn rate to narrow the valuation band.",
