      "narrative": "Apis Cor is a seed-stage housing and construction technology company that has raised $5.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of five private-stage companies in the same sector (BotBuilt, Unlimited Industries, Ground Control Development, ADMARES, and Hedral), as no public comparables exist in this subsector.\n\nThe stage-progression method applies a 2.5x multiplier to the $6M proxy value derived from total capital raised, a typical step-up from seed to the next funding round. This method yields an implied valuation of $14M. The analysis uses this single applicable approach as the foundation for triangulation given data constraints at the seed stage.\n\nThe resulting valuation range is $12M to $16M, with a median of $14M. This range reflects approximately \u00b115% sensitivity around the central estimate. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the five private comparables relative to Apis Cor's specific technology profile and market position, the appropriateness of the 2.5x multiplier given the company's trajectory and capital efficiency, and the absence of public market anchors in this emerging subsector. The median estimate should be treated as indicative pending deeper analysis of peer growth profiles and market traction metrics.",
