      "narrative": "SpliceBio is a Series B-stage biotech company founded by Miquel Vila-Perell that has raised $135M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 8 private companies and 3 public comparables in the Biotech & Health sector, including stage-adjacent firms such as Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), New Limit ($3.1B, Series C), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M, Series B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method, using the $135M total raised as a base value proxy and applying a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x, yields $256M. The peer-median method across the four sampled comparables produces a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M (floor) to $10.3B (ceiling). The public-comp anchoring approach cannot be applied because SpliceBio's revenue is not on file, precluding use of the sector P/S median of 6.2x.\n\nThe two applicable methods support a triangulated range of $218M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The wide dispersion reflects the stage heterogeneity of available peers\u2014three Series C comparables pull the median upward, while the single Series B peer (Eikon at $539M) sits well below. Key uncertainties include the applicability of later-stage valuations to a Series B context and the absence of SpliceBio-specific revenue or clinical-stage metrics that might narrow the range.",
