      "narrative": "Nomagic is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $97M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable, all operating in robotics and manufacturing at equivalent or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $97M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $184M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B). The median valuation across this set is $1.8B, with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide spread, reflecting tension between early-stage fundraising anchors and late-stage peer multiples. The triangulated analysis suggests a range of $157M (low, derived from stage-progression with downside adjustments) to $2.0B (high, peer ceiling), with a median of $967M. Key uncertainties include whether Nomagic's revenue, product maturity, or market traction justify positioning toward the upper peer range versus the stage-based lower bound. Resolution of these factors\u2014particularly evidence of defensible unit economics and customer concentration\u2014would narrow the band materially.",
