      "narrative": "Pragmatic Semiconductor is a Series D frontier-chip company founded by Richard Price and Scott White, having raised $231M to date. Valuation is anchored against a universe of 8 private frontier-semiconductor peers (including Tenstorrent, Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, and PsiQuantum) and 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $231M total raised proxy, yielding $346M. Peer-Median anchors to the median valuation across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers: Etched ($5.0B, Series E), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C), producing a median of $2.4B with a range of $529M to $5.0B. Public-Comp Anchoring cannot be applied because Pragmatic's revenue is not on file, though the public semiconductor sector trades at a 21.0x price-to-sales median.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $295M (low) to $2.7B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide dispersion reflects uncertainty around Pragmatic's relative positioning within the peer cohort and the stage-progression multiplier's applicability to frontier-stage capital efficiency. Revenue disclosure would materially narrow this range.",
