      "narrative": "Pulsar Fusion is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $15M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 4 same-sector peers at Series B and C stages (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse), with valuations ranging from $1.1B to $8.0B. Additionally, 5 public space and aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) provide sector context, though direct public comp anchoring is not applicable due to undisclosed target revenue.\n\nTwo valuation methods apply. The stage-progression method uses the $15M raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B progression, implying a valuation of $28M. The peer-median method anchors to the $1.6B median valuation across the 4 same-stage comparables, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B reflecting material dispersion within the cohort.\n\nTriangulating these two approaches yields a median valuation of $839M with a low of $24M and a high of $1.9B. The wide range reflects tension between early-stage funding metrics and peer-market precedent. Key uncertainties center on Pulsar Fusion's differentiated technology maturity, addressable market position within its peer set, and whether comparable company valuations reflect sustainable valuation multiples or sector-specific pricing dynamics.",
