      "narrative": "KrattWorks is a Series A defense and security company founded by Mattias Luha and T\u00f5nis Voitka, with reported revenue of \u20ac19.7M. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparable companies: 2 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms including Stark Defence, Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the \u20ac19.7M (~$20M) total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $39M. Peer-median valuation across three same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M)\u2014produces a median of $400M, with a full peer range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range: low of $33M, median of $220M, and high of $460M. The disparity reflects material uncertainty around which peer cohort most appropriately anchors valuation. Stage-progression implies modest valuation relative to capital deployed, while peer-median is heavily influenced by the $4.0B outlier. The $220M median balances both approaches but remains sensitive to peer selection and assumptions about KrattWorks' competitive positioning within a heterogeneous defense-tech landscape. Additional data on revenue growth trajectory, customer concentration, and technology differentiation would narrow this band materially.",
