      "narrative": "Unseenlabs is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac112.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 6 private comparables in the same sector and stage, spanning valuations from $1.15B to $8.0B, alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median price-to-sales multiple of 27.4x.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable to this target. The Stage-Progression method applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $112M total-raised proxy, yielding $191M. The Peer-Median method anchors to six same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014including Sierra Space ($8.0B), Apex Space ($2.3B), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B), Varda Space Industries ($1.6B), and Aalyria ($1.3B)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.8B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples is not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue data.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a range of $163M (low) to $2.1B (high), with a median of $991M. The wide spread reflects material dispersion in peer valuations and the stage-progression method's reliance on raised capital rather than operational metrics. Key uncertainties include revenue scale, customer concentration, and whether Unseenlabs' technology and market position warrant positioning toward the peer median or the lower quartile of the comp set.",
