      "narrative": "Cailabs is a Series C-stage frontier technology company in Space & Aerospace that has raised \u20ac57M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 6 private peers at similar or adjacent stages (Series B\u2013D) and 5 public Space & Aerospace companies, including Sierra Space, Apex Space, Varda Space Industries, and tickers RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, and SATL.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the \u20ac57M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, implies a value of \u20ac97M. The peer-median method across 6 same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of \u20ac1.8B, with a range from \u20ac1.15B (minimum) to \u20ac8.0B (maximum). The public-comp P/S approach cannot be applied due to unavailable revenue disclosure. The public Space & Aerospace sector trades at a median 27.4x price-to-sales.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods produces a range of \u20ac82M (low) to \u20ac2.1B (high), with a median of \u20ac943M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and scale variation within the peer set and uncertainty around Cailabs' revenue trajectory and market position within the sector. The stage-progression result sits materially below peer-based anchors, suggesting either compressed valuation relative to peers or incomplete fundraising disclosure. Key uncertainties include actual revenue run-rate, customer concentration, and whether comparable precedents fully reflect the target's specific technology positioning within Space & Aerospace.",
