      "narrative": "Beyond Aero, a Series A transportation-tech company founded by Eloa Guillotin, Hugo Tarl\u00e9, and Valentin Chomel, has raised $44M to date. The broader transportation frontier-tech sector includes 8 private peers (Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Pipedream, FleetZero among them) and no direct public comparables, limiting traditional multiples-based approaches.\n\nA stage-progression methodology, the only applicable triangulation method given data constraints, uses the $44M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage step-ups, yielding an $88M implied valuation. A peer-median approach was not viable: while three same-sector companies exist, none met minimum thresholds (\u22653 comparable datapoints) within the same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier. Applying an all-sector median would introduce unacceptable noise given transportation's idiosyncratic capital intensity and development timelines.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $75M to $101M, centered at $88M. Material uncertainties stem from the single-method derivation and the absence of narrow-set peer anchoring. The valuation is sensitive to (i) the applicability of a 2.0x stage multiplier\u2014which may vary by subsector within transportation\u2014and (ii) whether post-Series A capital needs and burn dynamics differ materially from peer norms. Further diligence on technology differentiation and unit economics relative to the private peer set would refine this range.",
