      "narrative": "Ephos is a seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Andrea Rocchetto, Francesco Ceccarelli, and Ciro Pentangelo, having raised \u20ac41.5M EU plus $8.5M in seed funding. The valuation universe comprises 3 public semiconductor comps (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private-stage peers including Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems.\n\nOne valuation method proved applicable to the available data. Stage-progression analysis uses Ephos's $42M total raised as a proxy for current implied valuation, then applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement in the sector, yielding $104M. Peer-median analysis was not executable\u2014while 12 same-sector peers exist in the Chips & Semiconductors universe, none of the filters (same stage, adjacent stage, similar valuation tier) yielded three or more comparable datapoints, making cross-firm median benchmarking unreliable. Public-comp anchoring, though supported by a 21.0x P/S median across the three public tickers, cannot be applied because Ephos's revenue is not on file, which is typical for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $88M to $119M, centered on $104M. The analysis rests on a single method, introducing material uncertainty around the final value. Key risks include the stage-progression assumption's applicability to frontier-tech semiconductors, the absence of granular private peer data, and the target's pre-revenue or early-revenue status, which limits market-based anchoring.",
