      "narrative": "AAVantgarde Bio is a Series B\u2013stage biotech company founded by Alberto Auricchio and Natalia Misciattelli that has raised $141M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 8 private peers and 3 public companies in the Biotech & Health sector, including same-stage and adjacent-stage companies such as Eikon Therapeutics ($539M), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $141M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $268M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 comparables yields a median valuation of $3.5B, with a range spanning $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not publicly available, limiting the utility of the 6.2x Biotech & Health P/S median observed across public tickers RXRX, TEM, and ONT.L.\n\nTriangulating these two methods yields a median estimate of $1.9B, with a low-end floor of $228M and a high-end ceiling of $4.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around AAVantgarde's clinical progress, regulatory pathway, and competitive position within the peer set. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively; peer-median relies on limited and highly dispersed comparables.",
