      "narrative": "Synspective is a publicly traded Space & Aerospace company founded by Motoyuki Arai. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage public comparables: Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across these 4 public Space & Aerospace peers is $5.2B, with a range spanning $840M to $40.0B. This dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in business model maturity, launch cadence, and market positioning within the sector. The public-comp anchoring method\u2014leveraging the Space & Aerospace sector P/S median of 27.4x across 6 traded tickers\u2014cannot be applied due to the absence of Synspective's revenue on file.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4.4B (low) to $6.0B (high), centered on the peer median of $5.2B. Key uncertainties include the company's revenue scale and profitability trajectory relative to the peer set, as well as the appropriateness of the selected comparables given Synspective's specific operational focus within Space & Aerospace. The wide dispersion among peers ($840M to $40.0B) signals that stage and sector membership alone are insufficient to pin valuation; deal-by-deal context on growth rate, margin profile, and capital intensity is material to narrowing the range.",
