      "narrative": "EX-Fusion is a Series A\u2013stage nuclear energy company founded by Kazuki Matsuo, Shinsuke Fujioka, and Yoshitaka Mori, having raised $37M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 private and 3 public peers in the nuclear energy sector, including Fuse Energy, Valar Atomics, Nano Nuclear Energy, and public-market comparables (OKLO, NNE, SMR).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $37M total raised as a base proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $74M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014produces a median valuation of $808M, with a range spanning $200M to $6.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $63M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $441M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and strategy heterogeneity within the nuclear energy peer set. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor given the company's early-stage capital position, while peer-median captures higher valuations observed in the sector. Key uncertainties include technology maturity and differentiation relative to peers, commercialization timeline, and the sustainability of elevated private nuclear valuations amid public-market volatility.",
