      "narrative": "Digantara is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $50M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws from a universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, Skyryse) and 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), supplemented by broader private-market intelligence across 8 additional frontier-tech space companies.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to the $50M raised as a proxy for current valuation, applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $95M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 identified comps produces a $1.6B result, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied\u2014the Space & Aerospace sector trades at a 27.4x median P/S across 6 tickers, but Digantara's revenue is not on file, precluding derivation.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce meaningfully different signals. Triangulating these results yields a low bound of $81M, a median of $872M, and a high of $1.9B. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: the stage-progression method assumes modest growth from current raise, while peer comparables incorporate substantially higher-valuation recent rounds in the sector. Resolution of this range depends on clarifying Digantara's revenue trajectory and competitive positioning within its subsector of space infrastructure.",
