      "narrative": "Sicona Battery Technologies is a Series A\u2013stage company in the Climate & Energy sector that has raised $22M+ to date. The comparable universe includes one public company (LNZA) and eight private peers spanning battery technology and critical materials, including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient granularity for a reliable median-based valuation; no same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tier exist in sufficient quantity to support a peer-multiple approach.\n\nThe analysis applies stage-progression methodology, which is applicable given Sicona's clearly defined Series A position. Using total raised ($22M) as a valuation proxy and applying a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to the subsequent financing stage yields an implied valuation of $44M. This single-method triangulation provides a central estimate with bounds: a low scenario of $37M reflects conservative adjustment, while a high scenario of $51M reflects more generous progression assumptions.\n\nThe valuation range supported is $37M\u2013$51M, with a median of $44M. Key uncertainties center on the absence of narrow peer benchmarks; any valuation outside this range would require either material new information on Sicona's technical differentiation or revised assumptions about stage-progression multier applicable in frontier battery technology. Sensitivity to financing-stage multiples and capital intensity in this subsector remains material.",
