      "narrative": "Ranovus is a Series D+ stage semiconductor company that has raised $236M in total capital, including a $36M strategic investment fund grant in August 2025. The target operates within a competitive Chips & Semiconductors sector comprising 12 same-sector peers, of which 3 are public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 are private. Notable private peers include Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, PsiQuantum, and Etched.\n\nTwo standard valuation triangulation methods were evaluated for applicability. Peer-median analysis proved inapplicable due to insufficient narrow-stage and comparable-tier peer data; while 12 same-sector companies exist, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier peers yielded fewer than three datapoints required for meaningful comparison. Public-comp anchoring was similarly not applicable because Ranovus's revenue is not on file, preventing application of the public Semiconductors P/S median of 21.0x observed across the three public tickers.\n\nThe absence of applicable quantitative triangulation methods reflects both the early-stage nature of frontier semiconductor ventures and limited disclosure in private markets. A defensible valuation range for Ranovus would require either: (i) disclosure of current-period revenue or bookings; (ii) identification of additional private peers with comparable financing history and stage; or (iii) forward-looking margin and exit scenario modeling. The $236M raised to date establishes a valuation floor but does not, in isolation, support a point estimate or range.",
