      "narrative": "Simera Sense is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $16.3M to date. Valuation analysis relies on a peer universe of 4 private companies at Series B/C stages (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse) plus 5 public comparables, given the frontier-tech nature of the sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $16M total raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B progression, implies a valuation of $31M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector private comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring using a 27.4x median price-to-sales multiple cannot be applied due to the absence of disclosed revenue for the private target.\n\nThe triangulated analysis implies a valuation range of $26M to $1.9B, with a median of $840M. The wide dispersion reflects fundamental uncertainty: stage-progression produces a conservative floor based on capital deployed, while peer-median anchoring captures significant heterogeneity within the space sector (illustrated by the $8B Sierra Space outlier versus the $1.1B Skyryse floor). Resolution of this gap depends critically on Simera Sense's revenue trajectory, customer traction, and technical differentiation relative to its peer set.",
