      "narrative": "Reflex Aerospace is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Walter Ballheimer, Alexander Genzel, and Christian Lindener, having raised \u20ac50M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only stage-progression anchoring proved applicable. This method uses the \u20ac50M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, yielding an implied valuation of \u20ac100M. Peer-median triangulation was not feasible due to insufficient datapoints within narrow Stage A, adjacent-stage, or similar-tier filters in the Space & Aerospace sector, despite 14 same-sector peers existing in the broader universe. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied because the target's revenue is not disclosed, which is standard for private companies; the public Space & Aerospace median P/S of 27.4x across six tickers cannot be meaningfully applied without this input.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac85M\u2013\u20ac115M, with a median of \u20ac100M. Key uncertainties include the absence of comparable private transaction data at identical stage and the lack of disclosed revenue metrics needed to anchor against public multiples. The single-method result warrants cautious reliance pending additional operational or financial disclosure.",
