      "narrative": "POLARIS Raumflugzeuge is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Alexander Kopp. The target operates within a sector comprising 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers, including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nPeer-median valuation proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow aerospace peer set. Of 14 same-sector peers identified, none satisfied the minimum threshold of 3 datapoints within matching stage and valuation tier bands. Public-comp anchoring could not be executed because the target's revenue figure is not on file, a common constraint for private companies. The public Space & Aerospace sector trades at a median P/S multiple of 27.4x across the 6 listed tickers, but this anchor cannot be deployed without revenue data from POLARIS.\n\nThe analysis framework identifies the key data constraints limiting quantitative valuation: absence of both target revenue disclosure and a sufficiently dense peer cohort at Series A within aerospace. Any valuation range would require either disclosure of POLARIS's revenue run-rate or identification of additional private aerospace comparables at the same funding stage. Until these gaps are filled, triangulation across standard VC methods is not supported by the available dataset.",
