      "narrative": "Monumo, a Series B semiconductor company founded by Martin Frost, Ian Murphy, and Dominic Vergine, is evaluated against a comp universe of 11 private peers and 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD). The company has raised $100M to date across its financing history.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. The Stage-Progression method, using total raised as a proxy base value of $100M and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $190M. The Peer-Median method anchors to four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series A), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series C), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C). The median valuation across this set is $1.5B, with a range spanning $529M to $11.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (median 21.0x across sector) cannot be applied without Monumo's revenue, which is not on file. The triangulated range derived from the two applicable methods spans $162M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $845M. Key uncertainty centers on the wide dispersion among peer valuations and stage mismatches within the comparison set, which materially widens the credible range.",
