      "narrative": "Vyoma is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac15M to date. The valuation exercise references a broader Space & Aerospace sector universe of 14 private peers and 6 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), though narrow peer matching proved constrained due to limited same-stage data density within the sector.\n\nThe primary applicable method is stage-progression analysis. Using the \u20ac15M total raised as a proxy baseline, application of a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement yields an implied valuation of \u20ac30M. The peer-median approach could not be reliably executed; while 14 same-sector private peers exist, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier cohorts failed to meet the minimum three-datapoint threshold necessary for statistical confidence. Public-comp anchoring proved inapplicable due to the absence of revenue disclosure\u2014standard for private companies and required to apply the 27.4x median P/S multiple observed across the six public Space & Aerospace names.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac26M (low) to \u20ac34M (high), with a median point of \u20ac30M. This narrow-method triangulation carries material uncertainty. The primary risk is reliance on a single methodology absent cross-validation from peer or public-market anchors. Revenue visibility and comparable transaction data at Vyoma's specific stage and subsector would materially sharpen the range.",
