      "narrative": "Space Machines Company is a Series A space & aerospace venture founded by Rajat Kulshrestha and George Freney, having raised AU$11M to date. The broader sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nOf the three standard valuation methods, only stage-progression analysis is applicable. This method uses the AU$11M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a typical 2.0x step-up multiplier from Series A to the next funding stage, yielding an implied valuation of AU$22M. Peer-median analysis cannot be performed because the narrow peer set filtered to same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables yielded fewer than three datapoints, making a median unreliable. Public-comp anchoring is inapplicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue figures for the target company; while the Space & Aerospace sector median trades at 27.4x revenue across the six public tickers, this multiple cannot be applied without revenue data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of AU$19M to AU$25M, with a median point of AU$22M. Key uncertainties stem from limited methodological corroboration\u2014only one method is defensible given data constraints\u2014and the absence of revenue disclosure, which prevents cross-validation through earnings or sales multiples common in mature sector analysis.",
