      "narrative": "Hyfix is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Mike Horton and Udan Ercan, having raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 peers (2 public, 8 private) in the same sector and adjacent funding stages, including comparable companies like UFORCE, Stark Defence, Singularity, and NODA AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A advancement, yielding $38M. Peer-median valuation across the four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps produces $700M, with the peer set ranging from $125M (NODA AI, Series A) to $4.0B (Stark Defence, Series A). The wide peer range reflects material variance in Defense & Security company maturity and product-market positioning at comparable stages.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $32M (low) to $805M (high), with a median of $369M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects two competing narratives: stage-based mechanics suggest modest progression from the $15M raised proxy, while peer comparables indicate significantly higher valuations for Defense & Security operators at Seed and early Series stages. Key uncertainties center on Hyfix's relative technical differentiation versus the peer set, customer traction beyond capital raised, and whether peer valuations reflect genuine market consensus or frothy sector dynamics.",
