      "narrative": "Scout Space is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company founded by Eric Ingram and Sergio Gallucci. The company has raised $18M to date. The applicable comp universe includes 5 public peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-stage frontier operators in space systems and launch services.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable method. Using the $18M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $36M. This method reflects normalized entry-valuation mark-ups observed in the sector. Peer-median triangulation could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables (0 same-stage, 2 adjacent-stage, all below the minimum threshold of 3). Public-comp anchoring using the Space & Aerospace sector median P/S of 27.4x across the 5-ticker public set is inapplicable without Scout Space's disclosed revenue.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $31M to $41M, centered on $36M. This range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue-based valuation anchors, a sparse private peer set at Scout Space's specific stage, and limited transparency into comparable Series A pricing for frontier aerospace ventures. A subsequent funding round or publicly disclosed financial metrics would materially reduce valuation dispersion.",
