      "narrative": "Rondo Energy is a Series B climate and energy company founded by John O'Donnell and Eric Trusiewicz that has raised $150M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 9 private and 1 public comparable company, with primary reference points including KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $150M total raised as a baseline proxy, applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $285M. The peer-median method anchors to the three most directly comparable same-sector, same/adjacent-stage firms, which trade at a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. This reflects material dispersion around earlier-stage capital intensity and differentiated market positioning within the climate tech sector.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $242M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $642M. The wide range reflects meaningful uncertainty around which peer comparables most closely reflect Rondo's market position and the degree to which stage-progression mechanics apply to frontier energy technology companies. Resolution of these uncertainties\u2014particularly relative competitive positioning within thermal energy and decarbonization end-markets\u2014will be material to precision of valuation as the company matures.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-08-19T10:30:46+00:00"
