      "narrative": "Thea Energy is a Series B nuclear energy company founded by Brian Berzin that has raised $20M to date. The valuation universe comprises 11 peers across the nuclear sector: three public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and eight private firms including Valar Atomics, X-Energy, Nano Nuclear Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable triangulation method here. Using total capital raised ($20M) as a proxy base value of $100M, and applying a typical Series B-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 1.9x, the method implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median comparison is not applicable due to insufficient comparable datapoints within nuclear energy at the same or adjacent stage; while five same-sector peers exist, filtering for comparable stage and valuation tier yielded fewer than three datapoints, making broad peer median unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M to $218M, with a median point estimate of $190M. This single-method result carries material uncertainty given reliance on stage-progression alone and the thinness of tight peer comparables in the nuclear subsector. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the $100M base proxy relative to Thea's specific technology maturity and market position, and whether the 1.9x multiplier accurately reflects Series B economics in frontier nuclear. A fuller view would benefit from additional public market data and resolution of Thea's technical differentiation within the nuclear competitor set.",
