      "narrative": "BRINC Drones, a Series C defense and security drone manufacturer founded by Blake Resnick, has raised $157M+ to date. Valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 13 same-sector companies at comparable or adjacent stages, comprising 2 public and 8 private comparables, supplemented by observation of top private peers including Quantum-Systems, Anduril Industries, and Helsing.\n\nTwo triangulation methods support the analysis. Stage-progression methodology, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $157M capital base, yields $267M. Peer-median analysis across the 13-company comp set produces $2.1B, with the peer range spanning $300M (low) to $18.0B (high). The peer cohort includes Quantum-Systems at $8.0B (Series C), Helsing at $18.0B (Series D), and Dream Security at $3.0B (Series B).\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a valuation range of $227M to $2.5B, with a median of $1.2B. The substantial spread reflects meaningful dispersion within the defense-tech peer set and uncertainty around BRINC's market position relative to better-capitalized competitors like Helsing and Quantum-Systems. Stage-progression alone anchors the lower bound; peer-median dominates the upper range. Key uncertainties include BRINC's revenue scale relative to peers and technology differentiation within a crowded frontier-defense ecosystem.",
