      "narrative": "Arena AI is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Pratap Ranade and Engin Ural that has raised $62M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies (2 public, 8 private) operating in the same sector and stage, including peers such as Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $62M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement to next-stage funding, yielding $118M. The peer-median method anchors to the median valuation of seven same-sector, same-stage comparables, which stands at $1.0B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B. This wide peer dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in deal quality and investor appetite within the defense AI subsector.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $100M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $559M. The substantial gap between the stage-progression floor and peer-median ceiling reflects structural uncertainty: Arena AI's relative market position, technology differentiation, and defense customer traction remain the primary determinants of whether the company tracks toward the lower or upper end. The peer range itself\u2014anchored by Dream Security at $3.0B\u2014suggests investor sentiment is highly dispersed on defense AI valuations at this stage.",
