      "narrative": "Cognichip is a Series A chip design company founded by Faraj Aalaei, competing in a deep peer set of 11 comparable companies\u20143 public (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private entities including SambaNova Systems, Cerebras, and Etched. The semiconductor sector P/S median across public comps stands at 21.0x, though application to Cognichip is not feasible given the absence of disclosed revenue for private companies.\n\nValuation analysis relies on a single applicable method: stage-progression anchoring. Using Cognichip's $93M total raised to date as a proxy for current value, application of a 2.0x step-up multiplier\u2014typical for Series A to next-stage advancement in capital-intensive sectors\u2014implies a valuation of $186M. This methodology assumes that capital deployed to date reflects investor conviction and relative positioning within the frontier-chip ecosystem.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $158M to $214M, centered on $186M. Critical uncertainties stem from the reliance on a single quantitative method; peer-median triangulation could not proceed due to insufficient same-stage or comparable-tier private companies with disclosed valuations. Public-comp anchoring remains inaccessible without revenue disclosure. The range reflects \u00b115% sensitivity around the stage-progression point estimate. Prospective investors should seek additional data on unit economics, patent composition, and customer traction to narrow this band.",
