      "narrative": "Deep Sentinel, a Series B defense and security company founded by David Selinger, has raised $55M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 10 comparables\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014all operating in the same sector and stage.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement to the $55M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $104M. The peer-median approach references 7 same-sector, same-stage private companies including Dream Security ($3.0B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), Castelion ($1.0B), and Defense Unicorns ($1.0B). This cohort yields a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $300M to $3.0B.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $89M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $552M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in peer applicability; peer valuations span more than a tenfold range, suggesting heterogeneous risk profiles or growth trajectories within the defense sector. The stage-progression method anchors conservatively below median, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher valuations. Resolution of this gap requires clarity on Deep Sentinel's revenue trajectory, market traction, and defensibility relative to the peer set.",
