      "narrative": "Tempo is a Series A climate and energy company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 9 private peers and 1 public comparable (Lonza, LNZA) in the climate and energy sector, including companies such as Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable approach. Using total capital raised of $50M as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $100M. Peer-median triangulation was not viable; while 9 same-sector peers exist, none of the narrow filters\u2014same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier\u2014produced the minimum three datapoints required for reliable median estimation. Reliance on broader sector medians would introduce unacceptable noise given stage and business model heterogeneity.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $85M (low) to $115M (high), with a median of $100M. This range reflects the limited methodological robustness afforded by a single applicable technique. Key uncertainties center on the representativeness of the 2.0x multiplier for this specific subsector and stage, and the absence of direct peer valuation anchors at identical stage and scale. Additional diligence on the company's capital efficiency, technical differentiation, and pathway to Series B would improve conviction in this range.",
