      "narrative": "Cambium, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Simon Waddington and Stephan Herrera, has raised $127M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public (277810.KQ) and 8 private\u2014including stage-matched peers Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised ($127M) as a proxy and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies $241M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B. The peer set reflects current market valuations for robotics companies at similar development stages.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $205M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $996M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around whether Cambium's metrics align with the lower end of stage-progression estimates or track closer to peer median multiples. Key sensitivities include revenue traction relative to peer cohort, capital efficiency post-Series B, and commercial deployment velocity in manufacturing automation. Further due diligence on unit economics and customer concentration would help narrow this range.",
