      "narrative": "JITX is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Jonathan Bachrach, Duncan Haldane, Austin Buchan, and Patrick Li, having raised $12M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private companies and one public entity across robotics and manufacturing.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $12M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implying a $24M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B, Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B, Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014yielding a median of $1.7B with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide triangulated range: low of $20.4M, median of $862M, and high of $2.0B. The stage-progression method yields a conservative floor consistent with capital deployed, while the peer-median result reflects downstream company valuations but is heavily influenced by Series B outliers. The critical uncertainty lies in appropriate peer stage adjustment; the four comps are predominantly Series B, one stage ahead of JITX's current position. A materially tighter range would require clarity on JITX's revenue traction, unit economics, and pathway to Series B fundraising, none of which are provided in the current dataset.",
