      "narrative": "JetZero is a Series B-stage transportation company founded by Tom O'Leary and Mark Page that has raised $1.0B+ to date. The transportation sector comprises 8 private peers (including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Arc Boats, and Parallel Systems) and no direct public comparables. The private peer set lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage datapoints to support median-based peer valuation, limiting triangulation to stage-progression methodology.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $1.0B total-raised proxy, yielding a $1.9B implied valuation. This single-method result anchors the analysis given the narrow peer universe and sparse transportation-sector comparables at JetZero's tier.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $1.6B (low) to $2.2B (high), centered on $1.9B median. This range reflects the inherent uncertainty of relying on one applicable methodology and the absence of narrow peer-valuation anchors. Key sensitivities include the appropriateness of the 1.9x multiplier to frontier-transportation dynamics and the assumption that total capital raised reasonably proxies for recent fair value. Materiality derives from comparable companies' stage transitions and sector-specific capital intensity, neither of which the current dataset quantifies with precision.",
