      "narrative": "X-Bow Systems is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Jason Hundley, Mark Kaufman, and Maureen Gannon, having raised $157M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 10 peers\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private companies in the same sector and stage, including Dream Security, Harmattan AI, Code Metal, Castelion, and Defense Unicorns.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis uses the $157M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $298M. Peer-median analysis examines seven same-sector, same-stage comparables, which span $300M to $3.0B with a median valuation of $1.0B. The peer range reflects meaningful dispersion in the defense-tech market; notably, Dream Security commands $3.0B while others cluster between $1.0B and $1.4B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $254M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $649M. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while the peer-median approach establishes the upper bound. Key uncertainties include X-Bow's relative competitive positioning within the peer cohort, the significance of capital efficiency versus absolute raised capital in the defense sector, and the degree to which the wide peer range ($300M\u2013$3.0B) reflects genuine business fundamentals versus valuation-stage timing effects.",
