      "narrative": "Viken Detection is a Series C defense and security technology company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 13 same-sector, same- and adjacent-stage private companies, supplemented by two public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). The private peer universe spans valuations from $300M to $18.0B, with named comparables including Quantum-Systems ($8.0B, Series C), Helsing ($18.0B, Series D), Saronic ($9.2B, Series D), Chaos Industries ($4.5B, Series D), and Dream Security ($3.0B, Series B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $50M total raised, implying a valuation of $85M. The peer-median method uses the median valuation across 13 same-sector comparables, yielding $2.1B, with a reported range spanning $300M to $18.0B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods produces a low bound of $72M, a median of $1.1B, and a high bound of $2.5B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty about whether Viken Detection's commercial traction and market position track toward the lower or upper quartile of the defense-tech peer set. Near-term revenue growth, customer concentration, and pipeline visibility would be critical inputs to narrowing this range.",
