      "narrative": "Western Chemicals is a pre-seed climate and energy technology company founded by Jared West (Columbia B.S. Physics and Mechanical Engineering, 2020), which has raised $175K to date. The sector peer universe consists of 9 private firms and 1 public company (Linz Textiles, LNZA), with notable private comparables including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen.\n\nValuation analysis relies on a stage-progression methodology, as peer-median approaches proved inapplicable. The climate and energy sector lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with adequate data density\u2014only three or more datapoints would support a reliable peer multiple. Accordingly, the stage-progression method applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier to the $175K total raised proxy, a typical advancement from pre-seed to next-stage funding, yielding an implied valuation of $438K.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $372K to $503K, with a median of $438K. This analysis is constrained by reliance on a single methodology; a peer-median cross-check cannot be credibly applied given the sparseness of directly comparable pre-seed transactions in climate tech. Key uncertainties include the sustainability of the 2.5x multiplier absent sector-specific pre-seed-to-seed progression data, and Western Chemicals' technical differentiation relative to better-capitalized peers in the sector.",
