      "narrative": "Citra Space Corporation is a Series A stage space and aerospace company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation universe comprises 5 public comps (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE, though the private peer set lacks sufficient granularity at identical stage and valuation tier for robust median-based anchoring.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for pre-money valuation and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent stage transitions, yields $30M. This represents the core quantitative anchor for the analysis. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (sector median: 27.4x across 6 public tickers) cannot be applied without the target's disclosed revenue. Peer-median triangulation is not reliable given insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparable transactions in the narrow Space & Aerospace cohort.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $26M to $34M, with a median point of $30M. This range reflects upside and downside variance around the stage-progression result, accounting for potential deal terms and relative positioning within the funding cycle. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue disclosure, limited transaction comparables at Series A in the sector, and reliance on a single methodology. Additional clarity on near-term revenue trajectory and unit economics would materially refine this range.",
