      "narrative": "Scale AI, a Series B AI & Software company founded by Alexandr Wang and Lucy Guo, is evaluated against a comp universe of 1 public peer (Palantir) and 8 private companies in the same sector, including Physical Intelligence, Black Forest Labs, and Field AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the company's last post-money valuation of $29.0B and a typical Series B step-up multiplier of 1.9x, implies a forward valuation of $55.1B. Peer-median analysis across three same-stage AI & Software peers yields a median valuation of $3.2B, with a range of $2.0B to $5.6B. The peer-median method reflects Physical Intelligence at $5.6B, Black Forest Labs at $3.2B, and Field AI at $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods produces a low estimate of $2.8B, a median of $29.2B, and a high of $63.4B. The substantial spread reflects a fundamental tension: the stage-progression method anchors to the company's most recent financing round, while the peer-median method suggests material downward pressure relative to that valuation. Key uncertainties include the applicability of stage-level multipliers to frontier-tech companies operating outside typical growth patterns, and whether recent peer valuations represent sustainable market pricing or reflect sector-specific momentum.",
