      "narrative": "Gallatin AI is a Seed-stage defense and security company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 private and 2 public firms operating in the Defense & Security sector, including same-stage and adjacent-stage peers such as UFORCE, Stark Defence, Singularity, and NODA AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $15M raised as a value proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $38M. Peer-median analysis across the four identified comparables yields a median valuation of $700M, with a range spanning $125M (NODA AI) to $4.0B (Stark Defence). The dispersion reflects heterogeneity in stage progression and operational maturity within the Defense & Security frontier-tech subset.\n\nThe two methods produce a triangulated range of $32M to $805M, with a median estimate of $369M. This wide band reflects material uncertainty about Gallatin's positioning relative to more mature Series A peers in the sample. The stage-progression method anchors a conservative floor; the peer-median is heavily influenced by outliers (UFORCE at $1.0B and Stark Defence at $4.0B). Key uncertainties include revenue traction, customer acquisition in defense procurement, and the company's technical defensibility relative to well-capitalized competitors. A narrower range would require additional operating metrics or customer concentration data.",
