      "narrative": "Perennial Autonomy operates in the Defense & Security sector at the government contract stage, backed by Schmidt and staffed with talent from SpaceX, Google, and Apple. The comparable universe spans 10 private firms and 2 public companies, including named peers Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems, alongside public reference points DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nPeer-median valuation methodology is not applicable here. The Defense & Security sector contains 23 total comparable companies, but filtering by stage, adjacent-stage proximity, or valuation tier yielded fewer than the three datapoints required for meaningful triangulation. An all-sector median approach would introduce material distortion given the sector's distinct risk, contract dynamics, and capital intensity. Without sufficient narrow-set peers, this method cannot support a defensible valuation range.\n\nThe analysis is therefore constrained by data availability rather than methodological option. Valuation support would require either: (1) disclosure of pricing multiples or recent fundraising terms from the named peer set, particularly Anduril, Helsing, or Shield AI at comparable stage; (2) public company margin or revenue multiples from DRSHF or IDEAFORGE.NS applied to Perennial's disclosed contract value; or (3) DCF informed by IDIQ deployment trajectory. The $500M IDIQ represents revenue potential, not current valuation anchor. Until additional comps data surfaces, no quantitative range can be responsibly derived.",
