      "narrative": "Cartesia is a Series B artificial intelligence and software company that has raised $186M to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of four same-stage, same-sector private peers\u2014Scale AI ($29.0B), Physical Intelligence ($5.6B), Black Forest Labs ($3.2B), and Field AI ($2.0B)\u2014alongside one public comparable (Palantir, ticker PLTR).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, anchoring to the $186M total raised and applying a typical 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $353M. The peer-median method, drawing on the four identified comparables, yields a median valuation of $4.4B, with a range spanning $2.0B to $29.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects material variance in company maturity and strategic positioning within the AI & Software sector at Series B stage.\n\nSynthesizing both approaches produces a triangulated valuation range of $300M (low) to $5.1B (high), with a median of $2.4B. The stage-progression method anchors the lower bound, while peer medians dominate the central estimate. Key uncertainties include the applicability of the Scale AI ($29.0B) outlier to Cartesia's specific technology and market position, and the degree to which revenue growth, product differentiation, and market timing support positioning within the observed peer range rather than toward the extremes.",
