      "narrative": "Portal Biotech is a Series A biotech company founded by Andy Heron and Giovanni Maglia that has raised $35M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a frontier-biotech comp universe comprising 3 public entities (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals.\n\nOnly one valuation method proved applicable given available data. Stage-progression anchoring uses the $35M total raised as a baseline proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to follow-on dynamics, yielding a $70M implied valuation. The peer-median method could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables in the biotech sector\u2014while 7 same-sector peers exist, filtering for stage, scale, and timing produced fewer than the three datapoints required for statistical reliability. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples (median 6.2x across the three public tickers) could not be deployed because Portal's revenue is not on file, a common constraint for private biotech companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $60M (low) to $80.5M (high), with a median estimate of $70M. This range rests entirely on stage-progression mechanics applied to deployed capital. Key uncertainties include Portal's burn rate, clinical-stage milestones, and IP differentiation relative to the private peer set\u2014factors that would meaningfully constrain or expand fair value within the stated band.",
