      "narrative": "ForSight Robotics, a Series B biotech & health company founded by Daniel Glozman, Joseph Nathan, and Moshe Shoham, is valued against a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit, and Eikon Therapeutics.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression, using the company's $195M total raised as a proxy and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $370M. Peer-median anchoring across four same-sector and same/adjacent-stage peers yields a median of $3.5B, with a range from $539M (Eikon Therapeutics) to $10.3B (Colossal Biosciences). Public-comp P/S anchoring is not applicable; while the Biotech & Health sector median trades at 6.2x revenue across the three public tickers, ForSight's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nTriangulating the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $315M (low) to $4.0B (high), with a median of $1.9B. The substantial spread reflects material uncertainty around ForSight's revenue traction, clinical pipeline maturity, and whether peer valuations in this sector reflect sustainable fundamentals or momentum-driven pricing. The Stage-Progression method's implied $370M sits below the peer-derived range and may underweight competitive positioning; the Peer-Median of $3.5B anchors to companies at Series C, one stage ahead. A narrow range would require revenue or clinical milestones not available in current data.",
