      "narrative": "Flamefront Propulsion is a pre-seed stage propulsion company in the Defense & Security sector, founded by Matt Garcia, former founding engineer and head of propulsion at Mach Industries with an MIT aeronautics background. The sector comprises 23 known peers, including 2 public companies (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private firms. Top-tier private comparables include Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, Saronic, and Quantum-Systems.\n\nPeer-median valuation methods cannot be reliably applied here. The Defense & Security sector lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables\u2014only one adjacent-stage peer was identified against a minimum threshold of three required datapoints. Broadening to all-sector medians would introduce unacceptable distortion given the specialized nature of defense propulsion versus broader defense applications. The sparse, heterogeneous comp universe at pre-seed stage precludes triangulation via this method.\n\nThe available evidence supports only qualitative positioning rather than a quantified range. Flamefront's founder pedigree\u2014established expertise in advanced propulsion from a recognized frontier player\u2014suggests a credible technical foundation for pre-seed funding, but without sufficient peer valuations, revenue multiples, or deal-stage benchmarks, deriving a defensible valuation multiple remains premature. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to the named private peers, revenue trajectory, and customer traction. A subsequent valuation round should await either expanded customer validation or new comparable transactions in frontier defense propulsion.",
