      "narrative": "Orqa is a Series A drone and autonomous systems company that has raised approximately $22M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of eight private-sector peers in Drones & Autonomous, including Zipline, Joby Aviation, Nuro, Archer Aviation, and Elroy Air. No public comparables exist in this narrow sector category.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the sole applicable triangulation method, uses the $22M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement. This yields an implied valuation of $44M. A peer-median approach could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within Orqa's specific tier\u2014while five peers operate in the broader Drones & Autonomous sector, none met the threshold of three datapoints at similar valuation stages needed for statistical reliability.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $37M to $51M, with $44M as the central estimate. Key uncertainties center on the scarcity of stage-matched private comparables, which limits triangulation to a single method. The wide band between low and high estimates ($14M spread) reflects this methodological constraint rather than high confidence in precise positioning within the range. Any valuation conclusion should be treated as provisional pending additional comparable transaction data or direct revenue and unit economics disclosure from the company.",
