      "narrative": "Oishii is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $385.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 9 peers spanning 8 private companies and 1 public listing, including same-stage peers Hadrian, Agile Robots, and Nimble Robotics.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach uses total capital raised as a proxy baseline ($386M) and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implying a valuation of $656M. The peer-median method benchmarks against three same-sector, same-stage competitors with a median valuation of $1.0B and range of $1.0B to $1.6B, directly implying $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a valuation range of $557M to $1.1B, with a median of $828M. The 97% spread between low and high estimates reflects material uncertainty around Oishii's relative competitive position versus the peer set. The Stage-progression method produces materially lower results than peer comparables, suggesting either that Oishii's capital efficiency or market position lags peers, or that the peer set commands sector-specific premiums. Key uncertainties include the timing and commercial traction relative to named competitors and applicability of public market multiples to the private peer base.",
