      "narrative": "Ohalo Genetics is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by David Friedberg and Judson Ward, having raised $205M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-stage, same-sector comparables\u2014Hadrian, Agile Robots, and Nimble Robotics\u2014supplemented by a broader universe of eight private robotics firms and one public comparable.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for post-money value, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $348M. The peer-median method references three direct comparables with a median valuation of $1.0B, ranging from $1.0B to $1.6B. These methods triangulate to a low of $296M, median of $674M, and high of $1.1B. The wide spread reflects material dispersion in the peer set, particularly the $600M gap between the stage-progression result and peer-median valuation. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 1.7x multiplier for this specific market cycle, whether the three peers represent true operational comparables, and revenue or growth metrics not provided in available data. The median estimate of $674M represents a reasonable midpoint, though confidence is constrained by the limited peer sample and reliance on raised capital as a valuation proxy.",
