      "narrative": "Shift5 is a Series C-stage defense and security technology company that has raised $180.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set of 13 same-sector peers at matching or adjacent stages, comprising 2 public companies and 8 private companies, with top-tier comparables including Quantum-Systems, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding an implied valuation of $307M. The peer-median method anchors to the median valuation across the 13-company comparable set, which stands at $2.1B, with observed peer valuations ranging from $300M to $18.0B. This wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity in company maturity and commercial traction within the defense-tech sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $261M (low) to $2.5B (high), with a median estimate of $1.2B. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects uncertainty around Shift5's positioning within its peer cohort. Key sensitivities include revenue scale relative to comparable companies, customer concentration in government contracts, and the trajectory of near-term fundraising. Resolution of these factors through operational milestones will be material to narrowing the range.",
