      "narrative": "nTop, a Series C robotics and manufacturing software company founded by Bradley Rothenberg and Greg Schroy, has raised $138.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 peers\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014across the robotics and manufacturing sector at similar stages, with primary peers including Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression modeling, using total capital raised ($139M) as a proxy base and applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C progression, yields $236M. Peer-median analysis across the 3 most recent same-stage comparables in the sector produces $1.0B, with a peer range of $1.0B to $1.6B. The median valuation across these two methods is $618M.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $201M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $618M. This wide range reflects a fundamental tension between nTop's capital efficiency relative to stage-appropriate benchmarks and the substantial valuations commanded by comparable robotics platforms. Key uncertainties include the stability of the peer comp set given rapid valuation movement in frontier robotics, the appropriate step-up multiplier for this sector, and the degree to which nTop's specific market position and product traction justify positioning toward the peer median versus below it.",
