      "narrative": "Viam is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Eliot Horowitz that has raised $117M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-stage, same-sector private companies (Hadrian, Agile Robots, Nimble Robotics) alongside one public comparable, supplemented by a broader universe of eight private peers in robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses total capital raised ($117M) as a value proxy and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implying a $199M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the three stage-matched comparables yields a $1.0B median valuation, with a range of $1.0B to $1.6B. The disparity between these methods reflects material differences in market positioning or growth trajectory relative to peers.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a low-to-high range of $169M to $1.1B, with a median of $599M. The wide spread reflects genuine uncertainty: the stage-progression method anchors conservatively to capital deployed, while peer-median extrapolates from a limited comparable set where valuations span 60% of the median. Key sensitivities include relative customer traction, deployment scale, and retention metrics versus the three primary comparables. A narrower range would require additional visibility into revenue, growth rates, or customer concentration versus peers.",
