      "narrative": "Somos is a Series B\u2013stage housing and construction company that has raised $105.6M to date. The comparable universe consists of four private peers in the same sector (Plantd Materials, Cuby Technologies, Cover, and Charge Robotics); no public comparables are available for direct benchmarking.\n\nThe valuation analysis applies a stage-progression method, using total capital raised ($106M) as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to subsequent-stage transitions. This yields an implied valuation of $201M. The methodology is constrained by the absence of public market data and limited private transaction history in the peer set, reducing confidence in the multiplier selection.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $171M (low) to $231M (median), centered on $201M. The wide band reflects methodological limitations rather than convergence across multiple independent approaches. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 1.9x multiplier for Somos' specific unit economics and market position, the relevance of the four private peers given potential heterogeneity in construction subsectors, and the absence of revenue or profitability metrics to anchor relative valuation. Additional transaction data or revenue-based comparables would materially improve precision.",
