      "narrative": "Cradle, a Series B biotech firm founded by van Grieken, de Reus, Prins, Bixby, and van Rossum, has raised $102.7M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 8 private and 3 public biotech companies, including Series B\u2013C peers like Eikon Therapeutics ($539M), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $103M raised proxy, yielding $195M. Peer-median anchoring across the four same-sector comparables produces $3.5B, with a range of $539M to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to lack of disclosed revenue data. The median across both methods is $1.8B, with triangulated estimates spanning $166M (low) to $4.0B (high), reflecting wide dispersion driven primarily by the outlier Colossal valuation and heterogeneity in peer maturity and capital efficiency.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of approximately $166M to $4.0B, with a median estimate of $1.8B. Key uncertainties include Cradle's capital deployment rate relative to peers, proprietary technology differentiation, and clinical or commercial traction not captured in fundraising alone. The wide range reflects material stage and scale variation within the peer set.",
