      "narrative": "Copia Automation is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $88.9M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014one public (ticker 277810.KQ) and eight private firms in the same sector and stage, including Hadrian, Agile Robots, and Nimble Robotics.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.7x multiplier to the $89M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $151M. Peer-median benchmarking across three same-stage robotics peers yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range of $1.0B to $1.6B. The peer-median method reflects the fact that comparable Series C robotics firms (Hadrian at $1.6B, Agile Robots and Nimble Robotics each at $1.0B) command substantially higher valuations relative to capital deployed.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $128M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $576M. The wide spread reflects material tension between the raised-capital proxy and peer multiples. Key uncertainties include whether Copia's revenue, unit economics, and market penetration justify peer valuations at the upper end of the range, versus a more conservative step-up multiple closer to historical progression. Revenue, runway, and customer concentration would be critical to narrowing this range.",
