      "narrative": "The Lumber Manufactory is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $53.1M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 9 private and 1 public peer, including same-stage companies Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applied. Stage-progression anchors to the $53M total raised and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C-to-next-stage advancement, implying a $90M valuation. Peer-median benchmarking against the three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a $1.0B implied value, with the peer range spanning $1.0B to $1.6B. The disparity between these methods reflects material uncertainty about the target's relative positioning within the robotics manufacturing cohort.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $77M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $545M. The wide spread\u2014driven by the 11x gap between stage-progression and peer-median methods\u2014reflects two competing narratives: either the target lags its peer set materially in progress, or the raised capital significantly understates economic value created. Resolution depends on nonpublic information regarding revenue, customer traction, and technical differentiation relative to Hadrian and peer cohort. The median of $545M should be treated as a point of central tendency rather than a point estimate without additional operational due diligence.",
