      "narrative": "Swift Solar, a Series C climate and energy company founded by Kevin Bush and five co-founders, has raised $52.7M to date. The valuation analysis draws on two methodologies triangulated against a peer universe of one public comparable (Lenza) and eight private climate-tech companies at similar stages, including KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nStage-progression analysis, applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $90M from the $53M raised proxy. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields $1.0B, reflecting the substantial range in the cohort: KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M. The peer-median approach captures broader market sentiment on frontier-energy valuations but exhibits significant dispersion.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $76M to $1.1B, with a median of $545M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty in several areas: the early-stage revenue profile and unit economics of Swift Solar relative to comparables; the maturity and technical differentiation of perovskite solar technology versus incumbent and competing next-generation approaches; and the timing and scale of commercialization. The stage-progression floor sits materially below peer-median estimates, suggesting either that peer valuations embed significant growth expectations or that Swift Solar's specific market position warrants a discount to sector medians.",
