      "narrative": "Vantage Robotics is a Series C defense and security robotics company that has raised $45.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 13 same-sector peers at Series B through Series D stages, including 8 private companies (Quantum-Systems, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and others) and 2 public comparables (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). The peer set spans valuations from $300M to $18.0B, with a median of $2.1B.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $45.6M raised as a baseline proxy, applying a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C to next-stage progression, yielding $78M. The peer-median method directly references the $2.1B median valuation across the 13 comparable companies at equivalent or adjacent stages. These methods produce significantly divergent results, reflecting both the early-stage nature of total capital raised relative to exit-ready valuations and the wide distribution of outcomes within the defense-tech peer set.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $66M (stage-progression floor) to $2.5B (peer-median ceiling), with a median of $1.1B. Key uncertainties include stage-specific valuation timing, capital efficiency relative to peers, and execution risk inherent to Series C defense-tech businesses. The wide range reflects sparse comparability at this stage and the pronounced variance in peer outcomes.",
