      "narrative": "Burro is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company founded by Terry Scott, Vibhor Sood, Charles Andersen, and Deniz Ilhan, having raised $44.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014including same-stage robotics firms Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $45M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yields $76M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same-stage comparables produces a $1.0B midpoint, with a range of $1.0B to $1.6B. The wider peer dataset (Divergent, Exotec, and others) confirms robotics-sector maturity at elevated valuations.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $65M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $538M. The significant spread reflects two divergent signals: stage-progression implies a conservative $76M, while peer-median suggests $1.0B as the central expectation. Key uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to named peers, product commercialization traction, and whether Burro's specific subsector within manufacturing robotics commands pricing at or below the peer median.",
