      "narrative": "Dimensional Energy is a Series A climate and energy company founded by Tobias Hanrath, Jason Salfi, David Erickson, and Clayton D. Poppe. The target operates within a frontier-tech sector characterized by a modest but growing public-private comp universe: one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. With $25.4M in total capital raised to date, the company sits at an early growth inflection point.\n\nValuation analysis employed stage-progression methodology, the only methodologically sound approach given available data. This method applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement dynamics to the $25.4M capital-raised proxy, yielding an implied post-money valuation of $51M. A peer-median approach was deemed inapplicable: while nine same-sector peers exist in the Climate & Energy universe, insufficient datapoints (fewer than three) met adjacent-stage or similar-tier filters necessary for statistical reliability. Applying a broader sector median would introduce unacceptable noise given the heterogeneity of frontier-energy business models.\n\nThe triangulated range is $43M\u2013$58M, with a central estimate of $51M. This reflects the single-method constraint. Key uncertainties include the applicability of 2.0x multipliers in deep-tech subsectors, the absence of tightly comparable staged peers, and macro fundraising environment shifts since the $25.4M raise. The range should be treated as preliminary pending acquisition of additional peer-stage transaction data or direct revenue/traction disclosure from the target.",
