      "narrative": "Nuview, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Clint and Katie Graumann, has raised $22.9M to date. The valuation landscape includes 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, though a sufficiently narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier does not exist to support median-multiple triangulation.\n\nStage-progression analysis, the sole applicable method, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement to the $23M raised proxy, yielding an implied valuation of $46M. This represents the primary quantitative anchor. Public-comp anchoring is not viable because Nuview's revenue is not disclosed, preventing application of the Space & Aerospace sector P/S median of 27.4x observed across listed peers. Peer-median analysis was also inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables meeting minimum threshold counts.\n\nThe triangulated range derived from available methods is $39M to $53M, with a median of $46M. This narrow methodological base\u2014relying on a single, mechanical stage progression rather than multiple independent approaches\u2014introduces material uncertainty. The valuation is sensitive to actual revenue performance, competitive positioning within a concentrated private peer set (SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, Planet Labs), and Series B market conditions. Without disclosed financials or a denser peer dataset, confidence in precision is appropriately limited.",
