      "narrative": "Matter, a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $21M, operates within a sector represented by 1 public comparable (277810.KQ) and 8 private peers including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics. The competitive landscape exists but remains sparse for direct valuation anchoring at this stage and scale.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. Using $14M as a proxy for total capital raised to date, a standard 2.5x multiplier applied to Seed-stage companies advancing to Series A yields an implied valuation of $35M. This methodology is grounded in observed step-up dynamics between early funding rounds but does not account for company-specific execution or market conditions. The Peer-Median method could not be applied: while 10 Robotics & Manufacturing companies exist in the broader comparison set, the narrow filters for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier peers yielded fewer than the three minimum datapoints required for statistical reliability. Broadening to sector-wide medians would introduce unacceptable heterogeneity.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $30M (low) to $40M (high), with a median point estimate of $35M. This range reflects the single applicable methodology and carries material uncertainty given the limited peer dataset and the inability to cross-check against comparable-company multiples. Key risks include competitive positioning within the robotics sector, capital efficiency trajectory post-Seed, and execution risk on core technology. The undisclosed current valuation prevents assessment of whether this range reflects recent fundraising activity.",
