      "narrative": "Teralta is a Climate & Energy frontier-tech company founded by Simon Pickup that has raised $15.8M to date. The valuation universe consists of 9 peers within Climate & Energy\u20141 public company (Lanzatech, ticker LNZA) and 8 private firms including Helion, Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, and Electric Hydrogen. The company's current stage and valuation remain undisclosed.\n\nThe peer-median method is not applicable to this analysis. A screen for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier comparables within Climate & Energy returned fewer than three datapoints in each category, rendering a narrow peer median unreliable. Drawing on the full sector median across all 9 Climate & Energy comps would introduce substantial survivorship and stage-mixing bias, as these peers span multiple funding rounds and market capitalizations.\n\nWithout sufficient cohort depth, traditional triangulation cannot be completed. Further valuation work would require either: (i) expansion of the comparable set to adjacent hard-tech sectors with documented stage and capital structure data, (ii) disclosure of Teralta's stage and any interim milestones to enable more precise peer filtering, or (iii) application of cost-of-capital or discounted cash flow methods if operating metrics become available. The $15.8M raised provides a floor on deployed capital but does not directly establish fair value.",
