      "narrative": "Aon3D is a Series C-stage robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $14.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (277810.KQ) in the robotics and manufacturing sector. Primary comparables include Hadrian ($1.6B), Agile Robots ($1.0B), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B), all at Series C stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $14.4M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $24M. Peer-median analysis references the three same-sector, same-stage comparables, which have a median valuation of $1.0B and a range of $1.0B to $1.6B, directly implying $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a wide range: $21M (low), $512M (median), and $1.1B (high). The substantial dispersion reflects tension between stage-progression mechanics applied to historical capital deployment and peer market valuations that have expanded significantly in the robotics sector. The $21M\u2013$1.1B spread underscores key uncertainties: the relevance of peer comparables given variation in technology maturity, customer traction, and burn profiles across the peer set, and whether Aon3D's specific competitive position and market opportunity justify positioning within the peer distribution. Analyst judgment on these factors is required to narrow the range.",
