      "narrative": "Pryzm is a seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Nick LaRovere, Matt Hawkins, David Istrati, and Justin Deckert that has raised $14.2M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector at seed and adjacent stages, including peers such as UFORCE, Stark Defence, Singularity, and NODA AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $14.2M total raised as a proxy base value and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a valuation of $36M. Peer-median methodology identifies four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with a median valuation of $700M, though the peer set exhibits substantial dispersion (range: $125M to $4.0B), reflecting heterogeneous risk profiles and capital efficiency within the defense-tech vertical.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a range of $30M to $805M, with a median of $368M. The wide dispersion between method results reflects two distinct narratives: stage-progression suggests a conservative $36M valuation anchored to capital deployed to date, while peer-median implies substantially higher value if Pryzm's technology or market position more closely resembles better-capitalized seed and series A peers. Key uncertainties include differentiation within a crowded frontier-defense cohort, customer traction relative to better-funded competitors, and whether peer valuations reflect durable defensibility or capital-driven inflation. Resolution of these factors is material to placement within the implied range.",
