      "narrative": "Laminar is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Annie Lu and David Lu, having raised $12.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine companies across robotics and manufacturing\u2014one public (277810.KQ) and eight private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, and Bedrock Robotics at comparable or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a valuation proxy, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A-to-next-stage advancement, implying a $25M valuation. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies yields a median valuation of $1.7B, with a range from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B). The latter method captures upside in a maturing robotics sector where comparable Series B companies command nine-figure valuations.\n\nThe triangulated range is $21M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $862M. This wide spread reflects the substantial stage and maturity variance within peer comparables\u2014particularly the inclusion of later-stage Series B companies\u2014and the inherent uncertainty in applying peer multiples to an early-stage, pre-revenue or nascent-revenue company. Key uncertainties include Laminar's specific traction metrics, capital efficiency relative to peers, and whether downstream Series B valuation benchmarks are appropriate given current operational stage.",
