      "narrative": "Kayhan Space is a seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Araz Feyzi and Siamak Hesar. The company has raised $12.1M to date. The comparable universe includes 5 public space and aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the only applicable triangulation approach given data constraints. Using total capital raised of $12.1M as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical for progression from seed to the subsequent financing stage yields an implied valuation of $30M. This method reflects how seed-stage companies in aerospace typically command a step-up upon advancing to Series A or equivalent rounds. The peer-median approach cannot be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow space and aerospace universe. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples is precluded by the absence of revenue disclosure, common among private companies at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $26M to $35M, with a median point of $30M. The primary uncertainty stems from reliance on a single methodology; validation would require either disclosure of target revenue against public multiples or identification of additional seed-stage private comparables with known valuations. The absence of narrower peer data limits confidence in any point estimate.",
