      "narrative": "Wraithwatch is a Seed-stage defense and security company founded by Nik Seetharaman, Savannah Grace Clemente, and Carlos M\u00e1s, having raised $8M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 4 same-sector and same/adjacent-stage comparables, supplemented by a broader universe of 10 private and 2 public defense-tech companies.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $8M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a typical Seed-to-next-stage multiplier of 2.5x, implying a $20M valuation. Peer-median analysis across 4 Defense & Security comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B, Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A)\u2014yields a median of $700M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis yields a low bound of $17M, a median of $360M, and a high bound of $805M. The wide dispersion reflects heterogeneity within the peer set, particularly the significant valuation variance between UFORCE and other Seed-stage entrants. Key uncertainties include whether Wraithwatch's product maturity and market traction align with high-valuation peers like UFORCE, or whether it trades closer to the lower quartile. Stage and funding trajectory will be material to convergence around the midpoint versus the extremes.",
