      "narrative": "Gambit is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Josh Giegel, Ben Richardson, and Andrew Kemendo that has raised $6.5M to date. The peer universe comprises 10 comparable companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private entities including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic\u2014spanning Seed and Series A stages within the same sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate Gambit's value. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 2.5x multiplier to the $6M raised as a proxy for current value, implying $16M. Peer-median analysis references four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Stark Defence at $4.0B, UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M), yielding a median valuation of $700M with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B. These methods produce a wide triangulated band: low of $14M, median of $358M, and high of $805M.\n\nThe significant dispersion reflects material uncertainty in stage-appropriate valuation for early-stage defense tech. The peer set's wide range\u2014particularly the $4.0B to $125M spread at comparable stages\u2014suggests sector valuation multiples remain volatile. Stage-progression suggests a more conservative $14M\u2013$16M range, while peer-median anchors toward $358M\u2013$700M. Without disclosed revenue or customer traction, the median estimate of $358M warrants caution; validation requires further disclosure of commercial progress or funding terms from subsequent rounds.",
