      "narrative": "Valstad is a Seed-stage company in Defense & Security founded by Dustin Walper that has raised $2.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 10 companies (2 public, 8 private) operating in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Shield AI, and Saronic.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $2.6M raised as a value proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression, implies a valuation of $6.5M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Stark Defence ($4.0B, Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A)\u2014yields a median valuation of $700M, with a range spanning $125M to $4.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide implied range of $6M to $805M, with a median of $353M. This dispersion reflects material uncertainty around whether Valstad's actual traction and defensibility warrant positioning in the lower quartile of the peer set (stage-progression view) or closer to median peers like UFORCE. The stage-progression method assumes minimal de-risking since formation; the peer-median approach depends critically on comparability assumptions given the wide spread ($125M\u2013$4.0B) within the peer set itself. Resolution of product-market fit and technical differentiation will be key to narrowing this range.",
