      "narrative": "The Spaceport Company is a seed-stage space and aerospace venture that has raised $2M to date. The valuation universe spans 14 private peers and 6 public comparables in the Space & Aerospace sector, including public companies such as Rocket Lab (RKLB), Planet Labs (PL), Lunar Outpost (LUNR), AST SpaceMobile (ASTS), and Satellite One (SATL), alongside private peers including SpaceX, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nOf three triangulation methods considered, only stage-progression analysis is applicable. This method applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression to the $2M total raised as a valuation proxy, yielding $5M. Peer-median analysis cannot be applied: while 14 same-sector private peers exist, none qualify as same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with sufficient data density. Public-comp anchoring is inapplicable because the target's revenue is not on file; the Space & Aerospace public median trades at 27.4x price-to-sales across five tickers, but without disclosed revenue this metric cannot be operationalized.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $4M to $6M, with a median point of $5M. This range reflects conservative downside ($4M) and modest upside ($6M) scenarios around the stage-progression result. Critical uncertainties include the absence of comparable seed-stage data within the narrow space sector, undisclosed revenue metrics, and limited visibility into capital requirements and market timing for the target's next financing event.",
