      "narrative": "Ghost Robotics is a Seed-stage defense and security robotics company that has raised $1.85M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable universe of 10 private and 2 public defense-tech firms, including peer companies Stark Defence ($4.0B Series A), UFORCE ($1.0B Seed), Singularity ($400M Series A), and NODA AI ($125M Series A).\n\nTwo valuation methodologies were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $1.85M total raised as a proxy for current value, applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression, yielding $4.6M. The Peer-Median method references the median valuation across the four comparable firms at $700M, reflecting the wide dispersion in the defense-tech sector (range: $125M to $4.0B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $4M to $805M, with a median of $352M. The wide divergence between stage-based ($4.6M) and peer-median ($700M) methods reflects material uncertainty: the Seed-stage model assumes limited prior validation, while peer comparables suggest significant market appetite for frontier defense robotics. Key uncertainties include Ghost Robotics' differentiation relative to better-capitalized competitors (Anduril, Shield AI, Helsing) and the pace toward revenue or material customer validation. The range is most reliable at the low end; valuations exceeding $200M would require demonstrated technical or market leadership not yet reflected in the available data.",
